const COMBINED_QUESTIONS = [{"id":"ml-1","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A partner wants to reuse a standard finance setup across many new customer companies without re-entering setup tables each time. Which Business Central tool is designed for this?","options":["A configuration (RapidStart) package exported as a .rapidstart file","A general journal batch","A security group","A financial report definition"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Configuration Packages","sub":null,"explanation":"After you set up a company that suits your needs, you can create a configuration (RapidStart) package containing the relevant setup data, then export it as a .rapidstart file and apply it when you create a new company that should be configured the same way.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"ml-2","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"In the configuration worksheet, how is the formatting hierarchy used to organize the tables you want to transfer to a new company?","options":["Tables contain areas, which contain groups","Areas contain groups, which contain tables","Groups contain areas, which contain tables","Packages contain questionnaires, which contain areas"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Configuration Worksheet","sub":null,"explanation":"Formatting in the configuration worksheet is based on a simple hierarchy: areas contain groups, which in turn contain tables. Areas and groups are optional but useful for arranging tables logically before adding the worksheet lines to a configuration package.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"ml-3","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Why can't you include the customer, vendor, and item ledger entry tables in a configuration package when migrating setup data?","options":["Those tables are always empty in a new company","You can't import data to tables that contain posted entries","Those tables are not part of the database schema","Ledger entry tables are encrypted and can't be exported"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Configuration Packages — Posted Entries","sub":null,"explanation":"You can't import data to tables that contain posted entries, like the customer, vendor, and item ledger entry tables. Don't include this data in a configuration package; instead post entries with journals after importing the package.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"ml-4","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"An administrator needs to turn an individual generally-available Copilot feature off for all users in a Business Central environment. Where do they do this?","options":["On the General Ledger Setup page","By deleting the user's permission set","On the Copilot & agent capabilities page, by selecting the feature and choosing Deactivate","In the Azure portal under Cognitive Services"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Copilot & Agent Capabilities","sub":null,"explanation":"On the Copilot & agent capabilities page, the administrator can select a feature in the list and choose Activate or Deactivate to turn it on or off for all users. Copilot is a system feature, so the page controls individual capabilities rather than Copilot as a whole.","source":{"title":"Configure Copilot and agent capabilities","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/enable-ai"}},{"id":"ml-5","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"The Allow data movement toggle appears on the Copilot & agent capabilities page. What does its presence indicate?","options":["The environment has exceeded its data storage quota","The Business Central environment is in a different geography than the Azure OpenAI Service that Copilot uses","Copilot has been permanently disabled by Microsoft","The company is using on-premises Business Central"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Copilot — Allow Data Movement","sub":null,"explanation":"The presence of the Allow data movement toggle indicates that the location of your Business Central environment differs from the Azure OpenAI Service geography that Copilot uses. To enable Copilot you must allow data movement across geographies.","source":{"title":"Configure Copilot and agent capabilities","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/enable-ai"}},{"id":"ml-6","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Two permission sets assigned to the same user both contain a security filter on the same table. How does Business Central combine them?","options":["It uses the most restrictive filter","It blocks access to the table entirely","The filters are combined so the least restrictive filter is used","Only the first permission set's filter applies"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1B","topic":"Permission Sets","sub":null,"explanation":"When multiple permission sets that refer to the same table data are assigned to a user, they're combined so that the least restrictive filter is used. You shouldn't repeat a table in multiple permission sets you plan to combine for one user.","source":{"title":"Using security filters","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/security/security-filters"}},{"id":"ml-7","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A consultant wants a salesperson to see only the records that contain a particular salesperson code. Which Business Central feature provides this record-level restriction?","options":["A global dimension","A security filter on the permission set's table data","A number series","A posting group"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1B","topic":"Security Filters","sub":null,"explanation":"Security filters provide record-level security. You set a security filter on a permission set's table data, choosing the field (such as Salesperson Code) and the value that limits the user's access to only those records.","source":{"title":"Using security filters","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/security/security-filters"}},{"id":"ml-8","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"What is the main advantage of using security groups rather than assigning permission sets to each user individually?","options":["Security groups bypass license entitlements","You can assign or change one permission set for many users in a single action","Security groups remove the need for permission sets","Only security groups support security filters"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1B","topic":"Security Groups","sub":null,"explanation":"Security groups make it easier to manage permissions: you organize users into groups and then assign or change one permission set for many users in one action. Permissions apply to all members of the group.","source":{"title":"Assign permissions to users and groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions"}},{"id":"ml-9","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"How many global dimensions and how many shortcut dimensions can you define on the General Ledger Setup page?","options":["Two global dimensions and eight shortcut dimensions","Eight global dimensions and two shortcut dimensions","Four global dimensions and four shortcut dimensions","Unlimited global dimensions and two shortcut dimensions"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1C","topic":"Global vs Shortcut Dimensions","sub":null,"explanation":"You can set up two global dimensions and eight shortcut dimensions. Global dimensions are used as filters on reports, batch jobs, and analysis views; shortcut dimensions appear as fields on journal and document lines.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"ml-10","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On the Dimension Combinations page, what does selecting the Blocked option for a combination of two dimensions mean?","options":["Both dimensions can be posted together, but only for certain dimension values","The two dimensions can't be posted on the same entry regardless of their values","The dimensions are hidden from all reports","The dimension values are deleted from the system"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1C","topic":"Blocked Dimension Combinations","sub":null,"explanation":"A blocked dimension combination means you can't post both dimensions on the same entry regardless of the dimension values. A limited combination, by contrast, allows both dimensions but only for certain value combinations.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"ml-11","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"An entry has more than one proposed default dimension because the customer account and the item account each carry a different default. How do you resolve which default applies?","options":["Block one of the dimensions","Set up default dimension priorities by source code","Delete the dimension from one of the accounts","Change the global dimension on the General Ledger Setup page"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1C","topic":"Default Dimension Priorities","sub":null,"explanation":"Different account types can have different default dimensions, so an entry might have more than one proposed default. You apply priority rules on the Default Dimension Priorities page per source code to avoid such conflicts.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"ml-12","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Before creating purchase approval workflows, what must you set up to define which sales and purchase records each approver is qualified to approve?","options":["A configuration package for each approver","An approver and substitute approver for each approval user, with amount limits","A separate company for each approval level","A security filter on the Workflow table"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1D","topic":"Approval Users","sub":null,"explanation":"Before you create approval workflows, you must set up an approver and substitute approver for each approval user. To define which records they're qualified to approve, you can also set amount limits for approvers.","source":{"title":"Walkthrough: Set up and use a purchase approval workflow","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/walkthrough-setting-up-and-using-a-purchase-approval-workflow"}},{"id":"ml-13","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Workflow approval notifications in Business Central are sent through which mechanism, which must be set up to start automatically?","options":["A Power BI dataflow","A job queue","A number series","The Adjust Exchange Rates batch job"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1D","topic":"Workflow Notifications","sub":null,"explanation":"All workflow notifications are sent through a job queue. You must make sure the job queue is set up to handle workflow notifications and that Start Automatically From Server is selected.","source":{"title":"Approval workflow notifications","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/across-setting-up-workflow-notifications"}},{"id":"ml-14","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When you run the Adjust Exchange Rates batch job, which exchange rate amounts on the Currency Exchange Rates page are used to update open bank, receivables, and payables transactions?","options":["The Exchange Rate Amount and Relational Exchange Rate Amount","The Adjustment Exch. Rate Amount and Relational Adjmt Exch. Rate Amt","The Fix Exchange Rate Amount only","The Unit-Amount Rounding Precision"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2A","topic":"Currency Exchange Rates","sub":null,"explanation":"The standard Exchange Rate Amount / Relational Exchange Rate Amount are used as defaults on new documents. The Adjustment Exch. Rate Amount and Relational Adjmt Exch. Rate Amt are used by the Adjust Exchange Rates batch job to update open bank, receivables, and payables transactions.","source":{"title":"Update currency exchange rates","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-how-update-currencies"}},{"id":"ml-15","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Why can't you link a currency code directly to a general ledger account in Business Central?","options":["G/L accounts can only hold foreign currency","Amounts on general ledger accounts are always in local currency (LCY)","Currency codes are reserved for bank accounts only","G/L accounts don't support posting groups"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2A","topic":"Currencies & G/L Accounts","sub":null,"explanation":"You can't link currency codes to G/L accounts because amounts on general ledger accounts are in LCY. Instead, you track foreign-currency balances on bank, customer, and vendor accounts; posting groups link those to the relevant G/L accounts where values show in LCY.","source":{"title":"Set up currencies","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-set-up-currencies"}},{"id":"ml-16","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A company wants every general ledger entry to be reported automatically in both LCY and a second currency. What should they set up?","options":["A unit-amount rounding precision","An additional reporting currency","A payment tolerance","A global dimension"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2A","topic":"Additional Reporting Currency","sub":null,"explanation":"By defining an additional reporting currency, amounts are automatically reported in both the local currency (LCY) and the additional reporting currency on each general ledger entry and on other entries.","source":{"title":"Setting up finance","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-setup-finance"}},{"id":"ml-17","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which G/L account type allows journals to post amounts directly to the account in the chart of accounts?","options":["Heading","Total","Posting","Begin-Total"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"G/L Account Types","sub":null,"explanation":"Each line in the chart of accounts is a G/L account of one of five types. Only Posting accounts allow journals to post lines to them; Heading, Total, Begin-Total, and End-Total define structure and subtotals for financial reporting.","source":{"title":"Understanding the Chart of Accounts","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-chart-of-accounts"}},{"id":"ml-18","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"How many top-level account categories does Business Central provide for mapping G/L accounts to build basic financial reports?","options":["Six: Assets, Liabilities, Equity, Income, Cost of Goods, and Expense","Four: Assets, Liabilities, Income, and Expense","Three: Balance Sheet, Income Statement, and Cash Flow","Five: Posting, Heading, Total, Begin-Total, and End-Total"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"G/L Account Categories","sub":null,"explanation":"You create the first layer of a financial report by selecting an account category for each G/L account. There are six categories: Assets, Liabilities, Equity, Income, Cost of Goods, and Expense.","source":{"title":"Organize general ledger (G/L) data using account categories","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/bi-account-categories"}},{"id":"ml-19","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A consultant wants to avoid creating a separate G/L account for every department and project. What is the recommended approach?","options":["Create a configuration package for each department","Use dimensions to categorize entries instead of expanding the chart of accounts","Use a separate company per department","Add more shortcut dimensions to the bank account"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"Dimensions vs Accounts","sub":null,"explanation":"Dimensions categorize entries so you can track and analyze them. Instead of setting up separate G/L accounts for each department and project, you use dimensions as the basis for analysis and avoid a complicated chart of accounts.","source":{"title":"Understanding the Chart of Accounts","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-chart-of-accounts"}},{"id":"ml-20","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On a sales document, which combination of posting groups determines the revenue (income statement) posting?","options":["The customer posting group and the inventory posting group","The general business posting group and the general product posting group","The bank account posting group and the FA posting group","The vendor posting group and the customer posting group"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"General Business vs Product Posting Groups","sub":null,"explanation":"The revenue posting is determined by the combination of the general business posting group (from the customer) and the general product posting group (from the item). The customer posting group determines the receivables (balance sheet) posting.","source":{"title":"Set up posting groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"ml-21","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which posting group defines the accounts to use when you post accounts receivable transactions for a customer?","options":["General product posting group","Inventory posting group","Customer posting group","Bank account posting group"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"Customer Posting Group","sub":null,"explanation":"Customer posting groups define the accounts to use when you post accounts receivable transactions. They are a specific posting group set up on the Customer Posting Groups page; the receivables posting on a sales document is determined by the customer's posting group.","source":{"title":"Set up posting groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"ml-22","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Inventory posting groups are assigned to items and then mapped to G/L accounts on which page, in combination with a location?","options":["General Posting Setup page","Inventory Posting Setup page","VAT Posting Setup page","Customer Posting Groups page"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"Inventory Posting Setup","sub":null,"explanation":"You assign inventory posting groups to items and map them to G/L accounts on the Inventory Posting Setup page. When you post an item entry, the system posts to the G/L account set up for the combination of inventory posting group and location.","source":{"title":"Set up posting groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"ml-23","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A company wants users to be able to choose a posting group other than a customer's default when working with a sales document. What must be enabled?","options":["The Allow Multiple Posting Groups toggle","The Automatic Cost Posting checkbox","The Force Doc. Balance field","The Direct Posting field on the G/L account"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"Multiple Posting Groups","sub":null,"explanation":"To let people choose alternative customer, vendor, or employee posting groups that replace the default, you turn on the Allow Multiple Posting Groups toggle on the relevant setup pages.","source":{"title":"Set up posting groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"ml-24","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"What is the relationship between a general journal template and a general journal batch?","options":["A batch contains many templates, each with its own page","A template defines the page and basic structure; you create one or more batches under it for personal layouts and number series","Templates and batches are identical and interchangeable","A batch defines the posting accounts; a template stores the journal lines"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Journal Templates vs Batches","sub":null,"explanation":"Each journal template is represented by a dedicated page with the functions and fields it needs. Under each template you set up one or more batches — for example a personal payment journal batch with its own layout, number series, and settings.","source":{"title":"Work with general journals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"ml-25","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"In a recurring general journal, how can you split a single posted amount across several different accounts?","options":["By creating a separate journal template for each account","By defining allocation lines with an Allocation %, Allocation Quantity, or Amount","By blocking the dimension combination","By posting the journal once per account manually"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Recurring Journal Allocations","sub":null,"explanation":"You can allocate an entry in a recurring general journal to several accounts by choosing the Allocations action and adding a line for each allocation, filling in the Allocation %, Allocation Quantity, or Amount field along with the account.","source":{"title":"Allocate recurring costs and income","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/year-allocate-costs-income"}},{"id":"ml-26","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On the General Journal Batches page, what does selecting the Suggest Balancing Amount checkbox do?","options":["It blocks posting until the journal balances by date","It prefills the Amount field with the value required to balance the document","It exports the batch to Excel","It assigns a number series to the batch"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Suggest Balancing Amount","sub":null,"explanation":"If you select Suggest Balancing Amount on the line for a batch, the Amount field on subsequent general journal lines with the same document number is automatically prefilled with the value required to balance the document.","source":{"title":"Work with general journals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"ml-27","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When applying a customer payment to multiple open customer ledger entries while posting a cash receipt journal, which action lets you select the entries to apply to?","options":["Insert FA Bal. Account","Apply Entries, then Set Applies-to ID","Calculate Inventory","Get Tables"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Cash Receipt Journal","sub":null,"explanation":"To apply a payment to multiple customer ledger entries when posting, you enter the full payment, choose the Apply Entries action, select the entries, and choose Set Applies-to ID before posting the cash receipt journal.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with a cash receipt journal","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"ml-28","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When the Application Method field on a customer card is set to Apply to Oldest, how are payments applied?","options":["Payments are never applied automatically","Payments are applied to the oldest open entry unless you manually specify an entry","Payments are applied to the newest open entry only","Payments are split equally across all open entries"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Application Method","sub":null,"explanation":"If the Application Method on the customer card contains Apply to Oldest, payments are applied to the oldest open entry unless you manually specify an entry. If the method is Manual, you always apply entries manually.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with a cash receipt journal","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"ml-29","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Why would a company assign more than one depreciation book to the same fixed asset?","options":["Each book must use the same depreciation terms","To calculate depreciation differently for different purposes, such as one for tax reporting and another for internal reporting","Because a fixed asset can't be acquired without two books","To split the asset into two physical components"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2D","topic":"Depreciation Books","sub":null,"explanation":"Depreciation books define the different ways depreciation is calculated. You can assign multiple depreciation books to a fixed asset for different purposes, for example one for tax reporting and another for internal reporting, each with its own terms.","source":{"title":"Set up fixed asset depreciation","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-depreciation"}},{"id":"ml-30","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which depreciation method depreciates the asset value with a fixed yearly percentage or amount evenly over the depreciation period?","options":["Declining-Balance 1","Straight-Line","Half-Year Convention","Declining-Balance 2"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2D","topic":"Depreciation Methods","sub":null,"explanation":"With Straight-Line depreciation you depreciate the asset value either with a fixed yearly percentage or a fixed yearly amount evenly over the depreciation period. Declining-balance methods allocate the largest part of the cost to the early years.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"ml-31","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"With the DB1/SL depreciation method, how does Business Central decide which amount to post each period?","options":["It always uses the straight-line amount","It always uses the declining-balance amount","It calculates both a straight-line and a declining-balance amount and posts the greater of the two","It averages the two amounts"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2D","topic":"DB1/SL Method","sub":null,"explanation":"DB1/SL combines Declining-Balance 1 and Straight-Line. The Calculate Depreciation batch job computes both a straight-line amount and a declining-balance amount, and only the greater of the two is transferred to the journal each period.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"ml-32","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A company sells items with a limited shelf life and wants the oldest goods sold first. Which costing method matches this assumption?","options":["LIFO","FIFO","Standard","Specific"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3A","topic":"Costing Method — FIFO","sub":null,"explanation":"FIFO assumes the first items placed in inventory are sold first, which suits items with a limited shelf life because the oldest goods need to be sold before they pass their sell-by date.","source":{"title":"Design details: Costing methods","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-costing-methods"}},{"id":"ml-33","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which costing method presets an item's unit cost based on an estimate, then adjusts to the actual cost later through variance values?","options":["Average","Specific","Standard","FIFO"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3A","topic":"Costing Method — Standard","sub":null,"explanation":"With the Standard costing method an item's unit cost is preset based on an estimate. When the actual cost is realized later, the standard cost must be adjusted to the actual cost through variance values. It's used where cost control is critical.","source":{"title":"Design details: Costing methods","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-costing-methods"}},{"id":"ml-34","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Under what condition can you NOT change an item's costing method?","options":["When the item has a variant","When item ledger entries already exist for the item","When the item is assigned to a location","When the item has an SKU"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3A","topic":"Changing Costing Method","sub":null,"explanation":"You can't change an item's costing method if item ledger entries exist for the item — that is, after you've bought or sold it. The recommended workaround is to replace the item with a new one and transfer inventory using an assembly order.","source":{"title":"Design details: Costing methods","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-costing-methods"}},{"id":"ml-35","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On the Inventory Setup page, which two fields must be filled to enable average cost calculation?","options":["Automatic Cost Posting and Expected Cost Posting to G/L","Average Cost Period and Average Cost Calc. Type","Costing Method and Unit Cost","Location Mandatory and Variant Mandatory"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3A","topic":"Average Cost Calculation","sub":null,"explanation":"Average cost is a periodic weighted average. Two fields on the Inventory Setup page enable it: Average Cost Period (Day, Week, Month, or Accounting Period) and Average Cost Calc. Type (Item, or Item/Variant/Location).","source":{"title":"Design details: Average cost","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-average-cost"}},{"id":"ml-36","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On a transfer order, when From Location and To Location have different default Department dimensions, which location's default dimension is copied?","options":["Always the From Location","The default from the last location field entered (the in-transit location is ignored)","Always the in-transit location","Neither — dimensions must be entered manually"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3B","topic":"Default Dimensions on Locations","sub":null,"explanation":"Because transfer orders deal with more than one location, the order of data entry matters: default dimensions are copied from the last location field entered, and the in-transit location is ignored.","source":{"title":"Set up locations","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-setup-locations"}},{"id":"ml-37","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which statement correctly distinguishes a sales line discount from a sales invoice discount?","options":["A line discount is a percentage off the whole document; an invoice discount is per line","A line discount applies to individual lines based on a combination such as customer/item/quantity; an invoice discount is a percentage subtracted from the document total when it exceeds a minimum","Both apply only to purchase documents","An invoice discount is an amount per line; a line discount is a percentage of the total"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3B","topic":"Line Discount vs Invoice Discount","sub":null,"explanation":"A line discount is given for lines based on a combination of customer, item, minimum quantity, unit of measure, or period. An invoice discount is a percentage subtracted from the document total if the sum of all lines exceeds a certain minimum.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"ml-38","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which setting makes Business Central automatically calculate invoice discounts on sales documents?","options":["The Allow Line Disc. toggle on the price list","The Calc. Inv. Discount toggle on the Sales & Receivables Setup page","The Discount Posting field on the General Posting Setup","The Best Price Calculation field on the item"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3B","topic":"Calc. Inv. Discount","sub":null,"explanation":"To have Business Central automatically calculate invoice discounts for sales, you turn on the Calc. Inv. Discount toggle on the Sales & Receivables Setup page, then define discount percentages per customer.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"ml-39","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A user wants to change records on a list page in Excel and push the updates back into Business Central. Which action should they use?","options":["Open in Excel","Edit in Excel","Enter analysis mode","Print to PDF"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Open in Excel vs Edit in Excel","sub":null,"explanation":"Both Open in Excel and Edit in Excel are available from the Share icon. Open in Excel exports a read-only view, while Edit in Excel lets you make changes to records in Excel and then update the data back in Business Central.","source":{"title":"View and edit in Excel from Business Central","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/across-work-with-excel"}},{"id":"ml-40","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"What is a key characteristic of the data analysis (analysis mode) feature on list pages?","options":["It permanently changes the underlying data of the list page","It analyzes data directly on the page without changing the underlying data or running a report","It requires exporting to Excel first","It is only available to delegated administrators"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Data Analysis Mode","sub":null,"explanation":"The data analysis feature lets you calculate, summarize, and examine data interactively directly from a list page or query, without running a report or opening Excel — and it doesn't change the underlying data or the page layout.","source":{"title":"Analyze list page and query data using data analysis feature","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/analysis-mode"}},{"id":"ml-41","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On a sales order, why can't you create an invoice for a quantity before it has shipped?","options":["Invoicing always happens automatically with shipment","Before you can invoice you must have recorded a shipment, or choose to ship and invoice at the same time","Sales orders never support partial invoicing","The Qty. to Invoice field is read-only on sales orders"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Sales Order — Ship before Invoice","sub":null,"explanation":"When you post a sales order you create a shipment and an invoice, together or independently. You can't create an invoice from the Sales Orders page for something that hasn't shipped — you must record a shipment first, or ship and invoice at the same time.","source":{"title":"Posting sales","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-post-sales"}},{"id":"ml-42","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"How do you create a partial shipment and a partial invoice from a single sales order?","options":["Split the order into two separate orders","Fill in the Qty. to Ship and Qty. to Invoice fields on the individual order lines before posting","Use the Combine Shipments batch job","Set the Shipping Advice field to Complete"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Partial Shipment & Invoice","sub":null,"explanation":"You can create a partial shipment and a partial invoice by filling in the Qty. to Ship and Qty. to Invoice fields on the individual sales order lines before you post. (Setting Shipping Advice to Complete actually prevents partial shipments.)","source":{"title":"Sell products with a customer sales order","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-sell-products"}},{"id":"ml-43","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"What is the purpose of a blanket sales order?","options":["To invoice multiple shipments on one document","To manage a customer's commitment to purchase large quantities delivered in several shipments over time","To reverse a posted sales shipment","To set up recurring sales prices"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Blanket Sales Orders","sub":null,"explanation":"A blanket sales order manages your customer's commitment to purchase large quantities delivered in several shipments over time. You convert blanket order lines into individual sales orders as deliveries are made.","source":{"title":"Sales","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/sales-manage-sales"}},{"id":"ml-44","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On a purchase order for items, what must happen before you can post a purchase invoice?","options":["You must record a receipt, or choose to receive and invoice at the same time","You must first create a blanket purchase order","You must run the Adjust Cost - Item Entries batch job","You must post the vendor payment"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Purchase Order — Receive before Invoice","sub":null,"explanation":"When you post a purchase order for items you can create a receipt and an invoice together or independently. You can't create a purchase invoice for products that aren't received — you must record a receipt first, or receive and invoice at the same time.","source":{"title":"Record purchases with purchase invoices and orders","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchases"}},{"id":"ml-45","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A drop-shipment sales shipment was posted but not yet invoiced. How can it be reversed?","options":["By deleting the posted sales shipment record","By opening the posted sales shipment and choosing Undo Shipment","By editing the Package Tracking No. field","By posting a negative quantity in the item journal"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4A","topic":"Undo Shipment / Reversal","sub":null,"explanation":"You can reverse posted drop shipments when both the sales shipment and the related purchase receipt aren't yet invoiced. You open the posted sales shipment and choose Undo Shipment; Business Central reverts the linked purchase receipt and creates correction entries.","source":{"title":"Make drop shipments","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-drop-shipment"}},{"id":"ml-46","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A customer received several separate shipments and should receive one invoice for all of them. Which feature accomplishes this?","options":["Recurring sales lines","Combine Shipments on a single invoice","Blanket sales order","Post Batch"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Combine Shipments","sub":null,"explanation":"The Combine Shipments feature lets you invoice a customer once for multiple shipments by combining the shipments on one invoice.","source":{"title":"Sales","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/sales-manage-sales"}},{"id":"ml-47","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"For critical fields on a posted sales document that affect the audit trail, how should corrections be made?","options":["Edit the posted document directly","Reverse or undo the posting rather than editing it","Delete the customer ledger entry","Change the value in the cash receipt journal"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Correcting Posted Documents","sub":null,"explanation":"You can edit certain noncritical fields on posted documents (such as Package Tracking No.). But for more critical fields that affect the auditing trail, you must reverse or undo the posting instead of editing it directly.","source":{"title":"Posting sales","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-post-sales"}},{"id":"ml-48","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Whether a separate G/L entry is posted for a sales discount amount depends on which setting?","options":["The Discount Posting field on the Sales & Receivables Setup page","The Direct Posting field on the G/L account","The Force Doc. Balance field on the journal template","The Allow Multiple Posting Groups toggle"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Discount Posting","sub":null,"explanation":"When a sales order is posted, posting might result in a G/L entry for the discount amount. Whether an entry for the discount is posted depends on the contents of the Discount Posting field on the Sales & Receivables Setup page.","source":{"title":"Posting sales","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-post-sales"}},{"id":"ml-49","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which page is one of the fastest ways to register payments by importing a bank statement file and automatically matching payments to open customer or vendor ledger entries?","options":["The Cash Receipt Journal page","The Payment Registration page","The Payment Reconciliation Journal page","The Bank Account Reconciliation page"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Payment Reconciliation Journal","sub":null,"explanation":"The Payment Reconciliation Journal page imports a bank statement file or feed and applies payments to open customer or vendor ledger entries based on data matches. You can review and change matches, and the bank account is reconciled when all payments are applied.","source":{"title":"Managing receivables","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-manage-receivables"}},{"id":"ml-50","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which page do you use to reconcile a bank account by matching imported bank statement lines with your system's bank account ledger entries, but where you can't apply payments?","options":["Payment Registration page","Bank Account Reconciliation page","Cash Receipt Journal page","General Journal page"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Bank Account Reconciliation","sub":null,"explanation":"On the Bank Account Reconciliations page you reconcile bank accounts by matching imported bank statement lines with your bank account ledger entries (and can reconcile check payments). You can't apply payments there — that's done in journals like the Payment Reconciliation or Cash Receipt journal.","source":{"title":"Managing receivables","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-manage-receivables"}},{"id":"ml-51","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When you correct (unapply) an application of customer entries, what happens to the entries that the original application closed?","options":["They are permanently deleted","Correcting entries with opposite-sign amounts are posted and the closed entries are reopened","Only the payment discount is reversed","The customer card is blocked"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Unapply Entries","sub":null,"explanation":"When you correct an application, correcting entries are created and posted for all entries — the same as the originals but with the opposite sign in the Amount field — and the entries that the application closed are reopened.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with a cash receipt journal","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"ml-52","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On a cash receipt journal line for a non-cash customer payment, what should the Bal. Account Type typically be set to?","options":["Fixed Asset","Bank Account","Customer","Item"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Cash Receipt Journal Accounts","sub":null,"explanation":"When posting a customer payment in the cash receipt journal you set Account Type to Customer and the Bal. Account Type to Bank Account for non-cash payments (or G/L Account for cash payments), then post the journal.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with a cash receipt journal","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"ml-53","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"What must you do before you can acquire a fixed asset in Business Central?","options":["Post a disposal entry","Set up and assign a depreciation book to the fixed asset","Run the Calculate Depreciation batch job","Block the asset for posting"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Acquire Fixed Asset","sub":null,"explanation":"You must set up and assign a depreciation book to each fixed asset before you can acquire it. You then acquire it by posting an acquisition transaction from the Fixed Asset G/L Journal, or by using the Assisted Fixed Asset Acquisition page.","source":{"title":"Acquire fixed assets","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-acquire"}},{"id":"ml-54","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which statement is true about posting a fixed asset disposal?","options":["A disposal entry can be posted at any time before depreciation","A disposal entry must be the last entry posted for a fixed asset, and the total disposal amount must be a credit","Disposal entries are posted from the cash receipt journal","You can post only one disposal entry per asset, never partial"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Dispose of Fixed Asset","sub":null,"explanation":"A disposal entry must be the last entry posted for a fixed asset. For partially disposed assets you can post more than one disposal entry, but the total of all posted disposal amounts must be a credit amount. You post it from the Fixed Asset G/L Journal with FA Posting Type Disposal.","source":{"title":"Dispose of or retire fixed assets","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-dispose-retire"}},{"id":"ml-55","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When posting depreciation manually from the Fixed Asset G/L Journal, which action creates the second journal line for the balancing account set up for depreciation posting?","options":["Calculate Depreciation","Insert FA Bal. Account","Get Related Tables","Set Applies-to ID"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Post Depreciation","sub":null,"explanation":"After creating the line with FA Posting Type Depreciation, you choose the Insert FA Bal. Account action, which creates a second journal line for the balancing account set up for depreciation posting in the FA posting group.","source":{"title":"Depreciate or amortize fixed assets","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-depreciate-amortize"}},{"id":"ml-56","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which journal do you use to change attributes such as the location, bin, or dimensions on item ledger entries without changing quantities?","options":["The physical inventory journal","The item reclassification journal","The cash receipt journal","The recurring general journal"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Reclassification Journal","sub":null,"explanation":"To change attributes on item ledger entries — such as dimensions, or to transfer items by reclassifying bin and location codes — you use an item reclassification journal.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory using journals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"ml-57","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On the Physical Inventory Journal, what happens after you enter the actual counted quantities and choose Post?","options":["Nothing is recorded until you also run the cash receipt journal","Posting creates item ledger entries and physical inventory ledger entries reflecting the difference","The calculated quantities are recalculated and overwritten","The items are transferred to the adjustment bin only"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Physical Inventory Count","sub":null,"explanation":"When you enter the actual counted quantity in the Qty. (Phys. Inventory) field and post, Business Central adjusts inventory to reflect the difference between expected and actual quantities, creating item ledger entries and physical inventory ledger entries.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory using journals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"ml-58","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A physical count reveals differences caused by items posted with incorrect locations. How should these be corrected?","options":["Enter the differences directly in the physical inventory journal","Use a reclassification journal or a transfer order to redirect the items to the correct locations","Post a negative adjustment for the whole quantity","Delete the affected item ledger entries"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Misplaced Items vs Reclassification","sub":null,"explanation":"If the physical count reveals differences caused by items posted with incorrect locations, you should NOT enter those differences in the physical inventory journal. Instead use a reclassification journal or a transfer order to move the items to the correct locations.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory using journals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"ml-101","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When migrating master data such as customers and vendors into a new company, what feature provides a set of default settings automatically assigned to imported records?","options":["Configuration templates","Number series","Posting groups","Security groups"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Configuration Templates","sub":null,"explanation":"Configuration templates contain a set of default settings that are automatically assigned to records imported into Business Central. They facilitate importing master data such as customer and vendor information and are an alternative to cloud migration tools.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"ml-102","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which permission, in a user's Business Central account, allows them to configure Copilot and agent capabilities?","options":["DATA ANALYSIS - EXEC","SUPER permission (or an equivalent admin license such as Dynamics 365 Administrator)","Copilot Sys Features only","Direct Insert on the User Group Member table"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1A","topic":"Copilot — Administrator Requirements","sub":null,"explanation":"To configure Copilot and agent capabilities you need SUPER permission in your Business Central user account, or one of the admin licenses such as Internal BC Administrator or Dynamics 365 Administrator. Business Central doesn't yet offer object-level permissions for Copilot configuration.","source":{"title":"Configure Copilot and agent capabilities","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/enable-ai"}},{"id":"ml-103","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"A Team Member-licensed user is assigned the SUPER permission set. What limits what they can actually do?","options":["Nothing — SUPER overrides the license","The Team Member license entitlements still limit the user","Only security filters limit the user","The user is blocked from signing in"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1B","topic":"License Entitlements vs Permission Sets","sub":null,"explanation":"License entitlements are the broad filter for what a user can do, while permission sets are the fine-grained filter. Even with the SUPER permission set, a Team Member-licensed user is still limited by the Team Member license entitlements.","source":{"title":"Access controls for Dynamics 365 Business Central","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-sovereign-clouds/public/access-controls-d365-business-central"}},{"id":"ml-104","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Why should you choose your global dimensions carefully to avoid changing them later?","options":["Global dimensions can never be changed once set","Changing a global dimension requires updating all entries posted with it, which can be time-consuming and lock tables","Changing a global dimension deletes all dimension values","Global dimensions are not used in reports"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1C","topic":"Changing Global Dimensions","sub":null,"explanation":"Changing a global or shortcut dimension requires all entries posted with the dimension to be updated. Using the Change Global Dimensions action can be time-consuming, affect performance, and lock tables during the update, so you should choose global dimensions carefully.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"ml-105","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On the Workflow Templates page, what does a workflow name that starts with the prefix 'MS-' indicate?","options":["The workflow is disabled","The template was added by Microsoft","The workflow requires Power Automate","The template is a Power BI report"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"1D","topic":"Workflow Templates","sub":null,"explanation":"Business Central includes many preconfigured workflows represented by workflow templates. When a template's name starts with MS-, it means the template was added by Microsoft. You can copy these templates to create new workflows.","source":{"title":"Workflows in Business Central","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/across-workflow"}},{"id":"ml-106","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When a currency adjustment triggers an unrealized gain at month-end and the actual payment is later registered at a different rate, where is the actual loss posted?","options":["To the inventory adjustment account","To the realized losses account, after the unrealized transaction is reversed with the payment","To the customer posting group's receivables account only","To the additional reporting currency account"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2A","topic":"Realized Gains/Losses","sub":null,"explanation":"At month-end a currency adjustment can trigger an unrealized gain. At payment time, the unrealized transaction is reversed together with the payment, and the actual loss is posted to the realized losses account.","source":{"title":"Currencies in Business Central","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-currencies"}},{"id":"ml-107","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"After mapping all chart-of-accounts G/L accounts to categories and subcategories, which action updates the built-in financial reports with that mapping?","options":["Get Tables","Generate Financial Reports","Adjust Exchange Rates","Calculate Inventory"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"Generate Financial Reports","sub":null,"explanation":"After you set up categories and subcategories and map all accounts, you choose Generate Financial Reports on the G/L Account Categories page. This updates the M-prefixed financial reports with the mapping for your chart of accounts.","source":{"title":"Organize general ledger (G/L) data using account categories","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/bi-account-categories"}},{"id":"ml-108","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On the General Posting Setup page, what is configured for each combination of general business and general product posting groups?","options":["A set of general ledger accounts to post to, such as sales and COGS accounts","The depreciation method for fixed assets","The number series for documents","The security filter for the table"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2B","topic":"General Posting Setup","sub":null,"explanation":"The General Posting Setup combines business and product posting groups; for each combination you assign a set of general ledger accounts to post to. This lets the same item post sales/COGS to different accounts depending on the customer's business posting group.","source":{"title":"Set up posting groups","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"ml-109","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which feature on the General Journal Batches page validates a finance journal while you work on it, showing issues in the Journal Check FactBox before posting?","options":["Suggest Balancing Amount","Background Error Check","Force Doc. Balance","Preview Posting"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Background Error Check","sub":null,"explanation":"On the General Journal Batches page you can choose Background Error Check to have Business Central validate finance journals while you work on them. The Check Document / Journal Check FactBoxes then show issues in the current line and the whole batch.","source":{"title":"Work with general journals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"ml-110","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When you apply a customer invoice in one currency to a payment in another currency, which date determines the exchange rate used for conversion?","options":["The work date","The posting date of the applying entry (Entry A)","The due date of the invoice","The last adjustment date of the currency"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2C","topic":"Cross-Currency Application","sub":null,"explanation":"When applying ledger entries in different currencies, the posting date on the applying entry (Entry A) is used to find the exchange rate that converts amounts on the other entry. Application of entries in different currencies must first be enabled.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with a cash receipt journal","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"ml-111","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"When the Half-Year Convention is turned on for a fixed asset, how much depreciation is taken in the first fiscal year?","options":["A full year regardless of the starting date","Six months of depreciation, regardless of the Depreciation Starting Date","No depreciation in the first year","Depreciation proportional to the exact starting date"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"2D","topic":"Half-Year Convention","sub":null,"explanation":"When you apply the Half-Year Convention method, a fixed asset has six months of depreciation in the first fiscal year, regardless of the contents of the Depreciation Starting Date field. It can be used with Straight-Line, Declining-Balance 1, and DB1/SL.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"ml-112","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Why is the LIFO costing method disallowed in many countries/regions?","options":["It requires serial number tracking","It can be used to depress profit","It only works with standard cost items","It can't be combined with locations"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3A","topic":"LIFO Costing","sub":null,"explanation":"LIFO assumes the last items placed in inventory are sold first. When prices are rising, the value on the income statement decreases, lowering tax liabilities. Because it can be used to depress profit, LIFO is disallowed in many countries/regions.","source":{"title":"Design details: Costing methods","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-costing-methods"}},{"id":"ml-113","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"On a customer card, what does the Invoice Disc. Code field reference?","options":["A number series for invoices","An existing customer whose invoice discount terms are reused","A posting group for receivables","A dimension value for the customer"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3B","topic":"Invoice Discount Codes","sub":null,"explanation":"Invoice discount codes are represented by existing customer cards. By selecting another customer's code in the Invoice Disc. Code field, you quickly assign that customer's invoice discount terms, which saves time when many customers share the same terms.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"ml-114","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"After special prices and line discounts are set up for sales and purchases, what does Business Central do automatically on documents and journal lines?","options":["It blocks the document until prices are confirmed","It calculates the best price on sales and purchase documents and on project and item journal lines","It removes all discounts above a threshold","It posts the discount to a separate company"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"3B","topic":"Best Price Calculation","sub":null,"explanation":"After you record special prices and line discounts for sales and purchases, Business Central automatically calculates the best price on sales and purchase documents and on project and item journal lines, helping ensure optimal profit.","source":{"title":"Record special sales prices and discounts","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-record-sales-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"ml-115","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Where do you access the posting options related to prepayments when processing a sales order?","options":["Only on the Sales Invoices page","Under the Posting menu of the sales order, which includes prepayment-related options","On the General Ledger Setup page","From the Payment Reconciliation Journal"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4B","topic":"Prepayments","sub":null,"explanation":"When posting a sales order, the Posting menu offers actions such as Post, Post and Send, Preview Posting, and Post Batch. For sales orders you can also access options related to prepayments (invoicing prepayments) from there.","source":{"title":"Posting sales","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/ui-post-sales"}},{"id":"ml-116","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","question":"Which two methods can you use to transfer inventory items between locations?","options":["Transfer orders and the item reclassification journal","Cash receipt journals and the physical inventory journal","Configuration packages and number series","Posting groups and dimension priorities"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"confidence":"high","set":null,"section":"4C","topic":"Transfer Orders vs Reclassification","sub":null,"explanation":"You can transfer inventory items between locations using transfer orders (to manage warehouse activities) or with the item reclassification journal, which can reclassify bin and location codes.","source":{"title":"Manage inventory","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-manage-inventory"}},{"id":"gen-1","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A functional consultant is standing up a brand-new Business Central tenant for a customer and wants to be guided through the essential configuration such as company details, communication information, and posting details rather than filling every setup page manually. Which tool provides this step-by-step guided experience?","options":["The Company Setup assisted setup guide","The Chart of Accounts wizard on the General Ledger Setup page","A recurring general journal batch","The Item Templates page"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Assisted setup guides walk you through configuring core areas of Business Central, and the Company Setup guide collects company, address, and posting details step by step. Other pages configure individual areas but do not provide the guided company onboarding experience.","source":{"title":"Get Business Central ready for business — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/setup"}},{"id":"gen-2","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During implementation you open the Assisted Setup list to see which guided setups are still outstanding for the company. Which statement best describes how assisted setup guides behave in Business Central?","options":["They can only be run once and disappear permanently after the first completion.","They must be purchased separately from AppSource before they appear.","They replace all manual setup pages, which become read-only afterward.","They are grouped by category on the Assisted Setup page and can be rerun to change earlier choices."],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Assisted Setup page lists guided setups grouped by category and shows which are completed; most can be run again to revise the choices you made. Manual setup pages remain available and editable after a guide runs.","source":{"title":"Get Business Central ready for business — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/setup"}},{"id":"gen-3","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to create an additional company inside an existing Business Central environment and pre-fill it with a set of standard configuration such as a chart of accounts and posting groups. Which option in the Create New Company assisted setup guide should be selected to include sample-style setup data?","options":["Create a company with no data, then import a database backup","Advanced Evaluation, which always deletes existing companies first","Evaluation - Sample Data or Production - Setup Data Only, depending on how much data is wanted","None; new companies can only ever be created empty"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Create New Company guide offers company templates such as Evaluation (with sample data) and Production - Setup Data Only, letting you decide how much predefined configuration and data to include. This is done through the guide, not by restoring a backup.","source":{"title":"Create new companies in Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/about-new-company"}},{"id":"gen-4","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After creating a new production company that contains only setup data, the customer needs their real customers, vendors, and items loaded. Within the Create New Company flow, what is the recommended way to bring in this master data?","options":["Retype every record manually because import is not supported for new companies","Copy the SQL database file directly into the tenant","Enter the records only through the Company Setup guide's address fields","Use the guide's option to import business data, for example via a configuration package or Edit in Excel"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"After a company is created, the recommended approach is to import business data using tools such as RapidStart configuration packages or Edit in Excel, rather than re-keying every record. The guide points to these data-migration options.","source":{"title":"Create new companies in Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/about-new-company"}},{"id":"gen-5","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A partner has built a reusable set of configured tables, field mappings, and default values that they want to apply to every new customer's company to speed up migration. Which Business Central feature is designed for packaging and reapplying this standardized configuration?","options":["Job queue entries","Report layouts","RapidStart configuration packages","Shortcut dimensions"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"RapidStart Services configuration packages let you collect tables, fields, and data into a reusable package that can be exported and imported to configure new companies quickly. Job queues, layouts, and dimensions serve unrelated purposes.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"gen-6","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"While preparing a RapidStart implementation, a consultant uses a page to organize the tables to be configured, assign responsibility, and track migration status for the new company. Which page is this?","options":["The Configuration Worksheet","The General Ledger Setup page","The Company Information page","The Number Series Lines page"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Configuration Worksheet is the central RapidStart page for organizing the tables to configure, grouping them, assigning responsibilities, and tracking migration progress before creating a configuration package. The other pages configure specific functional areas.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"gen-7","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to share a completed configuration package with a colleague who is implementing a similar customer on a different environment. In what form is a configuration package exported so it can be imported elsewhere?","options":["As a Word template (.dotx) file","As a printout that must be re-entered by hand","As a Power BI dataset","As a RapidStart package (.rapidstart) file"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Configuration packages are exported to a compressed .rapidstart file that can be imported into another Business Central company or environment to reapply the same configuration. Word templates and Power BI datasets are unrelated to this feature.","source":{"title":"Set up company configuration packages — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/set-up-standard-company-configuration-packages"}},{"id":"gen-8","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The customer wants sales invoice numbers to be assigned automatically in a continuous sequence such as INV0001, INV0002, and so on. Where does a functional consultant define the code, starting number, and increment for this sequence?","options":["On the No. Series page and its associated No. Series Lines","On the Report Layout Selection page","On the Job Queue Entries page","On the Dimensions page"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Number series are defined on the No. Series page, and the No. Series Lines specify the starting number, ending number, and increment. This is the standard mechanism for automatic document numbering.","source":{"title":"Create number series — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-create-number-series"}},{"id":"gen-9","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company has a rule that document numbers must never have gaps for audit purposes. Which No. Series Lines setting directly influences whether numbers can be skipped, producing gaps in the sequence?","options":["The Warning No. field","The Default Nos. checkbox on the series header","The Manual Nos. checkbox on the series header","The Allow Gaps in Nos. toggle"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Allow Gaps in Nos. setting on a number series line controls whether the sequence may skip numbers; enabling it improves performance but can create gaps, while disabling it keeps numbers strictly consecutive. Default Nos. and Manual Nos. govern how numbers are assigned, not gaps.","source":{"title":"Create number series — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-create-number-series"}},{"id":"gen-10","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer wants users to be able to accept the automatically assigned document number in most cases but occasionally type their own number on a specific document. Which combination of No. Series header settings supports this?","options":["Set Default Nos. to No and Manual Nos. to No","Set Default Nos. to Yes and Manual Nos. to Yes","Set Default Nos. to No and Manual Nos. to Yes only","Leave both blank, which forces manual entry everywhere"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Enabling Default Nos. makes the series assign numbers automatically, while enabling Manual Nos. permits a user to type a number instead when needed. Using both together gives automatic numbering with an optional manual override.","source":{"title":"Create number series — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-create-number-series"}},{"id":"gen-11","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On January 1 the customer wants sales orders to automatically switch from the SO-2025 series to a new SO-2026 series without editing setup pages that day. Which No. Series feature accomplishes an automatic switchover on a given date?","options":["The Where-Used list for the series","A job queue entry that renames the series","A relationship defined on the No. Series Relationships page combined with a Starting Date on the lines","The Allow Gaps in Nos. setting"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"You can add multiple lines to a number series with different Starting Date values so the series automatically begins using the next line's numbers on that date, and No. Series Relationships let one series roll into another. This enables a controlled annual switchover.","source":{"title":"Create number series — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-create-number-series"}},{"id":"gen-12","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is unsure whether it is safe to change the number series assigned to posted purchase invoices. Which action helps them see every place a particular number series is already assigned before making the change?","options":["Run the Where-Used action for the number series","Delete the series and recreate it","Export a configuration package of the whole company","Open the Report Layouts page"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Where-Used function shows all setup fields where a number series is referenced, so you can understand the impact before reassigning it. The other actions do not reveal where a series is used.","source":{"title":"Create number series — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-create-number-series"}},{"id":"gen-13","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer wants their printed sales invoice to use their own branding and layout designed in Microsoft Word. Which report layout type should the consultant create to let business users edit the design in Word?","options":["An RDLC layout","A Word layout","A configuration package layout","A security filter layout"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Word layouts are based on a Word document and are the recommended choice when business users need to edit the design in Microsoft Word. RDLC layouts require Report Builder/Visual Studio and are less accessible to end users.","source":{"title":"Manage report layouts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-manage-report-layouts"}},{"id":"gen-14","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The finance manager wants a sales invoice report to always print using the company's custom layout rather than the built-in default. Which page does the consultant use to assign the specific layout that a report should use?","options":["The Report Layout Selection page","The No. Series page","The Job Queue Entries page","The Configuration Worksheet"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Report Layout Selection page lets you choose which layout a given report uses per company, so a custom layout can replace the default. The other pages control numbering, scheduling, and RapidStart configuration.","source":{"title":"Manage report layouts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-manage-report-layouts"}},{"id":"gen-15","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is reviewing the layout types available for documents in a current Business Central version. Besides Word and RDLC, which additional built-in layout type can be used for reports?","options":["PowerPoint layouts","Visio layouts","Access layouts","Excel layouts"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central supports Word, RDLC, and Excel layouts (as well as externally defined layouts), with Excel layouts enabling data-analysis-style report output. PowerPoint, Visio, and Access are not report layout types.","source":{"title":"Manage report layouts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-manage-report-layouts"}},{"id":"gen-16","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer needs a heavy inventory valuation report to run at 2:00 AM every night automatically and the results emailed to the accountant. Which Business Central feature should the consultant configure to schedule this recurring background processing?","options":["A number series relationship","A report layout selection","A job queue entry","A configuration package"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Job queue entries schedule reports, codeunits, and batch jobs to run automatically in the background, including on a recurring schedule. This is the correct tool for automating a nightly report run.","source":{"title":"Schedule tasks with job queues — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/admin-job-queues-schedule-tasks"}},{"id":"gen-17","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant has created a job queue entry but it never runs. Which condition most directly prevents a job queue entry from executing on its schedule?","options":["Its status is set to On Hold rather than Ready","It has a description filled in","It is assigned an object type of Report","It uses a recurring rather than a one-time schedule"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A job queue entry only runs when its status is Ready; if it is On Hold it will not execute until it is set back to Ready. Having a description, targeting a report, or being recurring do not stop it from running.","source":{"title":"Schedule tasks with job queues — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/admin-job-queues-schedule-tasks"}},{"id":"gen-18","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer wants a job queue entry to run every weekday but not on Saturday or Sunday. Which settings on the job queue entry let the consultant control this recurrence pattern?","options":["The Allow Gaps in Nos. and Starting Date fields","The Recurring Job checkbox together with the day-of-week and Starting Time fields","The Default Nos. and Manual Nos. checkboxes","The Report Layout and Company Name fields"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Marking the entry as a Recurring Job exposes fields for the days of the week to run and the starting/ending time, so you can restrict it to weekdays. Numbering and layout fields are unrelated to scheduling recurrence.","source":{"title":"Schedule tasks with job queues — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/admin-job-queues-schedule-tasks"}},{"id":"gen-19","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A new employee needs access to Business Central. Their identity already exists in Microsoft 365 with an assigned Business Central license. What is the recommended way to bring this person into the Business Central environment so that their license and entitlement are respected?","options":["Manually create a user record on the Users page and type in their name and email","Use the Get New Users from Microsoft 365 action on the Users page to import them","Add them directly in SQL Server Management Studio","Create a new Windows account on the server hosting Business Central"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"In the online service, users are created in the Microsoft 365 admin center and then imported into Business Central using Get New Users from Microsoft 365, which pulls their license-based entitlement so permissions match their assigned license.","source":{"title":"Create users according to licenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-how-users-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-20","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In Business Central online, what ultimately determines which base permission sets (entitlements) a user is allowed to have?","options":["The user's assigned Microsoft 365 license","The Role Center chosen on the user's profile","The company the user logs into first","The number series assigned to the user"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"License-based entitlements are derived from the user's Microsoft 365 license (for example Essential or Premium); the license defines the maximum set of permissions the user can be granted.","source":{"title":"Create users according to licenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-how-users-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-21","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to build a custom permission set that is nearly identical to an existing Microsoft-provided one, changing only a few object permissions. What is the most efficient approach?","options":["Edit the Microsoft-provided permission set directly in place","Delete the system permission set and recreate it from scratch","Copy the existing permission set to a new user-defined one and modify the copy","Export the permission set to Excel and re-import it under a new name only"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"System (Microsoft-provided) permission sets are read-only. You copy one to create an editable user-defined permission set, then adjust the object permissions on the copy.","source":{"title":"Define granular permissions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-22","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On a permission set line, what does setting the Read permission to Yes but leaving Insert, Modify, and Delete blank grant the user for that object?","options":["Full control including the ability to add and remove records","The ability to view records but not to create, change, or remove them","The ability to modify existing records only","No access at all until Insert is also granted"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Granular permissions are set per object per action. Granting only Read allows the user to view data for that object while preventing insert, modify, and delete operations.","source":{"title":"Define granular permissions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-23","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user is assigned two permission sets: one grants Modify on the Customer table and another grants only Read on the same table. What effective permission does the user have on the Customer table?","options":["Read only, because the most restrictive permission wins","Modify, because permissions from multiple sets are combined (additive)","No access, because the two sets conflict and cancel out","Modify, but only in the company where the second set was assigned"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Permissions across assigned permission sets are cumulative. The user gets the union of granted permissions, so Modify from one set applies even though another set grants only Read.","source":{"title":"Define granular permissions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-24","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to verify exactly what a specific user can do with a specific object, taking all assigned permission sets into account. Which tool should they use?","options":["The Effective Permissions page","The Change Log Setup page","The Job Queue Entries page","The Configuration Worksheet"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Effective Permissions page shows the combined result of all permission sets assigned to a user for a given object, letting you troubleshoot and even temporarily override permissions.","source":{"title":"Define granular permissions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-25","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A sales manager should only be able to see and work with customer records assigned to their own salesperson code, even though they have Read and Modify permissions on the entire Customer table. Which feature enforces this record-level restriction?","options":["A shortcut dimension on the customer card","A security filter on the permission set line for the Customer table","A separate number series for each salesperson","A blocked posting group"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Security filters are applied on permission set lines to limit which records within a table a user can access, restricting data at the row level based on field values such as salesperson code.","source":{"title":"Using Security Filters — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/security/security-filters"}},{"id":"gen-26","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A security filter has been applied so a user can only access records where Location Code is BLUE. When the user tries to open a record for location RED, what happens?","options":["The record opens but all fields are greyed out","The user is prompted to enter an administrator password","The record is hidden and treated as if it does not exist for that user","The record opens normally because filters only affect reports"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A security filter restricts the records a user can read or act on; records outside the filter are effectively invisible to the user, as though they are not present in the table.","source":{"title":"Using Security Filters — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/security/security-filters"}},{"id":"gen-27","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An administrator wants to manage Business Central access for a whole department at once by tying it to an existing Microsoft Entra (Azure AD) group. Which Business Central feature supports this?","options":["Configuration packages","Security groups","Number series relationships","Analysis views"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Security groups let you link a Business Central security group to a Microsoft Entra group (or Windows group on-premises) and assign permission sets to the group, so membership and access are managed centrally.","source":{"title":"Control Access Using Security Groups — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-security-groups"}},{"id":"gen-28","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When using security groups in Business Central, how are permission sets granted to the individual members?","options":["Each member must still be assigned the permission sets one by one","Members automatically receive SUPER permissions","Permission sets are assigned to the security group, and members inherit them through membership","Permission sets are assigned per document rather than per group"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"You assign permission sets to the security group itself; any user who is a member of the linked group inherits those permission sets, simplifying administration for many users.","source":{"title":"Control Access Using Security Groups — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-security-groups"}},{"id":"gen-29","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A profile (role) determines what a user sees when they sign in to Business Central. Which of the following does assigning a profile to a user primarily control?","options":["The base license entitlement of the user","The security filters applied to the Customer table","The number series used for sales orders","The Role Center and the personalized page layout the user sees"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Profiles (roles) map users to a Role Center and its associated navigation and page customizations, defining the user experience rather than data-level permissions.","source":{"title":"Manage users and roles — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/admin-users-profiles-roles"}},{"id":"gen-30","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An administrator wants every accountant to open Business Central with the same tailored home page and navigation without each user personalizing it. What is the most efficient approach?","options":["Ask each accountant to personalize their own Role Center individually","Grant each accountant the SUPER permission set","Create a separate company for the accounting department","Customize the pages for the relevant profile so all users assigned that profile get the layout"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"On the Profiles (Roles) page you can customize pages for an entire profile; all users assigned that profile inherit the customized Role Center and layout, avoiding per-user personalization.","source":{"title":"Manage users and roles — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/admin-users-profiles-roles"}},{"id":"gen-31","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user reports they cannot see a page action that a colleague with the same profile can see. Both have identical permission sets. What is the most likely cause?","options":["The user has applied a personalization that hides the action","The user's Microsoft 365 license expired that morning","The action is blocked by a posting group","The user is in a different security filter"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Individual personalization can hide fields and actions for a single user. Because permissions and profile match the colleague, a personal customization hiding the action is the likely cause, and clearing personalization restores it.","source":{"title":"Manage users and roles — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/admin-users-profiles-roles"}},{"id":"gen-32","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In a multi-company Business Central environment, an administrator wants a user to have the Accountant permission set only in Company A but not in Company B. How can this be achieved?","options":["Permission sets are always global and cannot be limited to one company","Create a separate license for each company","Delete the user from Company B entirely","Assign the permission set to the user with the Company field set to Company A"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"When assigning permission sets to a user, you can scope the assignment to a specific company (or leave it blank for all companies), so the same user can have different access per company.","source":{"title":"Define granular permissions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-33","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which statement best describes the difference between a security group and a profile in Business Central?","options":["A security group controls permissions/data access; a profile controls the Role Center and UI experience","Both control only the visual layout of pages","A profile grants table permissions while a security group hides fields","They are two names for the same feature"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Security groups are used to assign permission sets (what a user can access) to groups of users, whereas profiles determine the Role Center and page experience users see when signing in.","source":{"title":"Control Access Using Security Groups — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-security-groups"}},{"id":"gen-34","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An administrator wants to review which users exist and confirm their license state and permission set assignments in a Business Central online environment. Which page provides this central overview?","options":["The Chart of Accounts page","The General Ledger Setup page","The Users page","The Item Journal page"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Users page lists all users, shows their license type and state, and is where you review and assign permission sets and security groups for each user.","source":{"title":"Create users according to licenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-how-users-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-35","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A developer defines a security filter using a table filter expression on a permission set line. In which filtering mode does Business Central enforce the filter so users cannot even read records outside it?","options":["Filtered mode is optional and only affects sorting","Security filters only apply when exporting to Excel","Security filters apply exclusively to the SUPER user","Security filters restrict which records a user can access for the operations granted, hiding the rest"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Security filters limit access to records that meet the filter criteria for the granted read/write operations; records not matching the filter are inaccessible to the user.","source":{"title":"Using Security Filters — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/security/security-filters"}},{"id":"gen-36","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After importing new users from Microsoft 365, a consultant notices they have no meaningful access beyond their base entitlement. What must the administrator do next to let them perform their job tasks?","options":["Assign appropriate permission sets (or add them to a security group) matching their responsibilities","Restart the Business Central service","Change the company's number series","Re-run the assisted company setup guide"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Importing users grants only license-based entitlements. To enable actual work, the administrator assigns task-appropriate permission sets directly or via a security group.","source":{"title":"Create users according to licenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-how-users-permissions"}},{"id":"gen-37","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to make a dimension available on the document and journal line fast entry, without needing to open the Dimensions FactBox, and also usable as a filter and column in the general ledger. Which type of dimension provides this direct field on lines and entries?","options":["A budget dimension","A blocked dimension value","An analysis view dimension","A shortcut dimension"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Shortcut dimensions appear as fields directly on document and journal lines so users can enter them without opening the full Dimensions page; up to eight can be set, two of which are the global dimensions.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-38","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In Business Central, how many global dimensions can be defined, and what is a key characteristic that distinguishes them from other shortcut dimensions?","options":["Exactly two, and you can filter and view them directly on entries and in reports and account schedules","Up to eight, and they can be changed on posted entries at any time","Exactly six, and they are only available in analysis views","Unlimited, and they replace the need for a chart of accounts"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central allows two global dimensions. They are automatically the first two shortcut dimensions and can be used as filters and in reports, account schedules, and batch jobs, unlike other shortcut dimensions.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-39","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer always incurs costs against the same department. The consultant sets a default dimension on the customer card and sets the Value Posting field to Same Code. What is the effect when a user posts a document for that customer with a different department dimension value?","options":["The system automatically replaces the entered value with the default value","Posting is allowed but the entry is flagged for review","The system prevents posting because the dimension value must match the specified default code","The dimension is ignored entirely on the posted entry"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A default dimension with Value Posting set to Same Code forces the entered dimension value to equal the specified default code; any other value blocks posting.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-40","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to require that every sales posting for a specific G/L account includes a value for the SALESCAMPAIGN dimension, though any value from that dimension is acceptable. Which Value Posting option should be set on the default dimension?","options":["Code Mandatory","Same Code","No Code","Blank"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Code Mandatory requires that a dimension value be entered (any valid value is accepted), whereas Same Code forces one specific value and No Code prohibits a value.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-41","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The controller does not want any dimension value to be posted for a particular balance-sheet G/L account. Which Value Posting setting on the default dimension enforces this rule?","options":["Code Mandatory","Same Code","No Code","Priority 1"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The No Code value posting rule prevents any dimension value from being used when posting to the account or entity to which the default dimension is assigned.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-42","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants a default department dimension applied to all customers at once rather than editing each customer card. Which action allows assigning default dimensions to a group of records of the same account type?","options":["Use the Default Dimension-Multiple action from the customer list","Create a new global dimension","Run the Analysis by Dimensions matrix","Change the shortcut dimension order in General Ledger Setup"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"From a list page you can select multiple records and use Dimensions, then Default Dimensions-Multiple, to assign the same default dimension to many accounts of the same type at once.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-43","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Two default dimensions with conflicting Value Posting rules could apply to the same posting — one from the customer and one from the G/L account. How does Business Central determine which rule wins when the account-type-default priorities are configured?","options":["The dimension entered most recently always wins","The rule from the source table with the highest assigned priority number is applied","The rule from the source with the lowest priority number (highest priority) is applied","Both rules are ignored and posting proceeds without dimensions"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Default Dimension Priorities let you rank source tables; the source with the lowest priority number has the highest priority, and its default dimension rule is applied when conflicts arise.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-44","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When setting up default dimension priorities, a consultant needs to group the priority rules so they apply only to a specific set of transactions. What identifier is used to group a set of default dimension priorities?","options":["A dimension combination code","A global dimension number","A blocking rule code","A source code / priority grouping code"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Default dimension priorities are grouped and identified by a source code so that the priority ranking applies to the relevant type of transaction.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-45","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company wants to prevent the DEPARTMENT value ADMIN from ever being combined with the PROJECT value that is used only for production work. Which dimension setup enforces that two dimension values cannot be used together?","options":["Configuring a Dimension Combinations rule as Blocked or Limited","Setting both values to Blocked","Assigning both to the same global dimension","Increasing the default dimension priority"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Dimension Combinations page lets you define whether two dimensions can be combined; setting a combination to Blocked prevents any values, and Limited restricts to specific value combinations.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-46","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On the Dimension Combinations page, a consultant sets the combination of the AREA and CUSTOMERGROUP dimensions to Limited. What does the Limited setting require the consultant to do next?","options":["Block all values of both dimensions from being posted","Open the Dimension Value Combinations page to specify which individual value pairs are allowed or blocked","Delete one of the two dimensions","Convert one dimension into a global dimension"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A Limited combination means only certain value pairs are permitted; you then use the Dimension Value Combinations page to define exactly which specific value combinations are allowed or blocked.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-47","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A dimension value named OLD-DEPT should no longer be used on new transactions, but historical entries that reference it must be preserved. Which setting on the dimension value prevents its future use without affecting posted history?","options":["Delete the dimension value","Set the Dimension Value Type to Blocked","Set the Blocked field on the dimension value to true","Remove it from the global dimensions"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Setting the Blocked field on a dimension value prevents it from being used in new postings while leaving existing posted entries that reference it intact.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-48","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is creating dimension values and wants some to act as subtotal or heading lines within reports rather than as postable values. Which property of a dimension value controls whether it can be posted to or serves as a total/heading?","options":["The Blocked field","The Value Posting field","The Global Dimension No. field","The Dimension Value Type field"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Dimension Value Type (Standard, Heading, Total, Begin-Total, End-Total) determines how a dimension value behaves — for example, headings and totals are not used for posting but structure reporting.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-49","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After go-live, management asks to swap one of the two global dimensions for a different dimension that is currently only a shortcut dimension. What is the correct consideration when changing a global dimension in a company with posted data?","options":["Global dimensions can be freely retyped in General Ledger Setup with no impact","Changing a global dimension is a resource-intensive operation performed with the Change Global Dimensions function, which updates existing entries","Global dimensions cannot be changed once any data is posted","You must first delete all analysis views before editing shortcut dimensions"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Changing global dimensions after posting requires the dedicated Change Global Dimensions process, which updates the global dimension fields on existing entries and can run in the background; it is a significant operation, not a simple field edit.","source":{"title":"Work with dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-50","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to combine dimensions with the amounts on G/L entries and view them in a matrix, filtering by dimension values and periods for reporting. Which feature is designed for this dimension-based reporting?","options":["Configuration packages","Analysis views and Analysis by Dimensions","Number series relationships","Default dimension priorities"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Analysis views let you analyze G/L data by dimensions, and the Analysis by Dimensions matrix presents the amounts across selected dimensions and periods for flexible reporting.","source":{"title":"Analyze data by dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bi-how-analyze-data-dimension"}},{"id":"gen-51","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An analysis view based on dimensions is not showing the most recent postings. What must be done to reflect the latest ledger entries in the Analysis by Dimensions matrix?","options":["Recreate the global dimensions","Block and unblock the dimension values","Change the analysis view to a different account type","Update (refresh) the analysis view so it includes newly posted entries"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Analysis views hold a copy of ledger data filtered by their dimensions; you must update the analysis view (manually or on a schedule) so that newly posted entries are included in the analysis.","source":{"title":"Analyze data by dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bi-how-analyze-data-dimension"}},{"id":"gen-52","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When defining an analysis view, which dimensions can be selected as the analysis dimensions for the view?","options":["Only the two global dimensions, and no others","Only dimensions that are blocked","All dimensions in the company automatically, with no selection possible","Up to four dimensions, which can include but are not limited to the global dimensions"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"An analysis view can include up to four dimensions of your choice for analysis, giving more flexibility than being limited to only the two global dimensions.","source":{"title":"Analyze data by dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bi-how-analyze-data-dimension"}},{"id":"gen-53","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user posted a general journal to a G/L account but forgot to include the required DEPARTMENT dimension value, and the entry is now posted. What tool does Business Central provide to add or correct dimensions on posted G/L entries?","options":["Delete and re-enter the G/L account","Use the Correct Dimensions feature to update dimensions on posted general ledger entries","Change the global dimension in General Ledger Setup","Reopen the fiscal year and repost the journal"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central lets you correct dimensions on posted G/L entries using the dimension correction functionality, so you can fix or add missing dimension values without deleting the entry.","source":{"title":"Troubleshoot and correct dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-troubleshooting-correcting-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-54","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant runs a dimension correction on posted G/L entries. What best describes how Business Central records the change so the audit trail is preserved?","options":["It silently overwrites the original dimension with no record of the change","It creates a dimension correction record that logs the before and after values, keeping traceability","It reverses and reposts the entire journal batch automatically","It removes the affected entries from the general ledger"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The dimension correction process stores a correction that captures the original and updated dimension values, preserving a full audit trail of what was changed on the posted entries.","source":{"title":"Troubleshoot and correct dimensions — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-troubleshooting-correcting-dimensions"}},{"id":"gen-55","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A functional consultant needs to enable document approvals in Business Central without any external services. Which built-in capability lets users route sales orders, purchase orders, and payment journals for approval directly inside Business Central?","options":["Native approval workflows","Power Automate cloud flows only","Job queue entries","Configuration packages"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central includes native approval workflows that combine tasks (such as document approval) into a connected process entirely within the application, without requiring Power Automate.","source":{"title":"Workflows in Dynamics 365 Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-workflow"}},{"id":"gen-56","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Before any approval workflow can be created and used, which prerequisite setup must a consultant complete so that requests can be sent to and acted on by the right people?","options":["Create a new number series for approvals","Set up workflow users in the Approval User Setup page","Enable the general ledger setup for background posting","Assign a dedicated permission set called WORKFLOW-ONLY"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Workflow (approval) users must be defined on the Approval User Setup page, mapping each user to an approver and defining approver chains and amount limits, before approval workflows can function.","source":{"title":"Set up approval workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-set-up-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-57","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In the Approval User Setup page, a consultant configures an amount above which a user's requests must be escalated to a higher approver. Which field controls this threshold?","options":["Unlimited Request Approval","Approval Administrator","Approval Limit (Amount Approval Limit)","Substitute"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Amount Approval Limit field on Approval User Setup sets the maximum amount a user can approve; requests above it are forwarded up the approver chain to a user with a higher or unlimited limit.","source":{"title":"Set up approval workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-set-up-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-58","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants the workflow to automatically send a request to a specific manager regardless of the requester's direct approver chain. Which approver type on the workflow response should be used?","options":["Approver (direct approver in the chain)","Workflow user group","Approval Administrator","Specific approver (a chosen approver)"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Setting the approver type to a specific approver lets you route the request to one designated user, rather than following the requester's approver chain or approver limits.","source":{"title":"Set up approval workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-set-up-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-59","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When building a workflow on the Workflow page, a consultant defines the logic in three linked columns. Which set correctly names these three building blocks in order?","options":["When Event, On Condition, Then Response","Trigger, Filter, Action","On Insert, On Validate, On Post","Start, Decision, Stop"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Each workflow step is defined by a When (event), On Condition, and Then (response) structure, chaining tasks together into a connected approval process.","source":{"title":"Create approval workflows to connect tasks — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-to-create-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-60","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The fastest way to create a working approval workflow for a standard scenario, such as purchase document approval, is to base it on which starting point?","options":["A blank workflow built entirely from scratch","A workflow template supplied with Business Central","A configuration package imported from Excel","A copied posted document"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central ships with predefined workflow templates for common scenarios; creating a workflow from a template pre-populates the events, conditions, and responses, which you then adjust.","source":{"title":"Workflows in Dynamics 365 Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-workflow"}},{"id":"gen-61","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A purchasing agent submits a purchase order for approval. What status does the document take on, preventing it from being posted until a decision is made?","options":["Released","Open","Pending Approval","Rejected"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"When a document is sent for approval, its status becomes Pending Approval, which locks it from editing and posting until the approver approves or rejects the request.","source":{"title":"Approve or reject documents in workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-use-approval-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-62","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An approver is on leave, and requests should temporarily be handled by a colleague without changing the workflow. Which approval action lets the approver reassign a specific pending request to another user?","options":["Cancel","Delegate","Reject","Reopen"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Delegate action reassigns an approval request to the substitute or another user so it can be acted on when the original approver is unavailable.","source":{"title":"Approve or reject documents in workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-use-approval-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-63","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A requester realizes an approval request was sent with an error and wants to edit the document again. Which action must the requester take on the pending document?","options":["Approve the request themselves","Delegate the request","Delete the workflow","Cancel the approval request"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The requester (sender) can cancel the approval request, which returns the document to Open status so it can be edited and resubmitted.","source":{"title":"Approve or reject documents in workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-use-approval-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-64","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is configuring how approvers are told about pending requests. Which setup determines the recipients and the message content for approval workflow notifications?","options":["Notification setup for the workflow's recipients (Notification Setup / notification entries)","The number series lines on the document","The dimension priority setup","The posting no. series on the journal batch"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Approval workflow notifications are configured through notification setup, which controls who receives notifications and how, so approvers know when action is required.","source":{"title":"Setting up approval workflow notifications — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-setting-up-workflow-notifications"}},{"id":"gen-65","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"To have approval notifications delivered on a schedule (for example, batched daily rather than instantly), which Business Central component must be configured to run the notifications?","options":["A recurring general journal batch","A job queue entry","A configuration worksheet","An analysis view update"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Scheduled notification delivery relies on a job queue entry that processes and sends the queued approval notifications according to the defined schedule.","source":{"title":"Setting up approval workflow notifications — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-setting-up-workflow-notifications"}},{"id":"gen-66","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant must decide between a native Business Central approval workflow and a Power Automate flow. Which statement best reflects when Power Automate is the appropriate choice?","options":["When approvals must stay entirely inside Business Central with no external services","When the process needs to connect Business Central with other apps and services outside it","When defining amount-based approver limits per user","When using the built-in workflow templates only"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Native workflows handle approvals within Business Central, whereas Power Automate is suited to scenarios that integrate Business Central with other applications and services beyond the app.","source":{"title":"Workflows in Dynamics 365 Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-workflow"}},{"id":"gen-67","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After defining a workflow's events, conditions, and responses, what must a consultant do before the workflow will actually run on documents?","options":["Post the workflow to the general ledger","Export the workflow as a configuration package","Select the Enabled check box on the workflow","Assign the workflow a number series"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A workflow is inactive until you turn on the Enabled toggle; only enabled workflows respond to the events they are built on.","source":{"title":"Create approval workflows to connect tasks — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-to-create-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-68","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In a workflow response, a consultant wants the system to send an approval request to the requester's direct manager and continue up the chain until someone with a high enough approval limit is reached. Which approver type supports this behavior?","options":["Salesperson/Purchaser","Workflow user group","Specific approver","Approver (approver chain based on approval limits)"],"correct":[3],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Approver type uses the approver hierarchy defined in Approval User Setup, forwarding the request up the chain until it reaches an approver whose amount limit covers the request.","source":{"title":"Set up approval workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-set-up-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-69","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A manager reviews a pending sales order and decides it should not proceed. After the manager rejects it, what happens to the document?","options":["It is automatically posted with a warning","It returns to Open status so the requester can edit or resubmit it","It is permanently deleted from the system","It advances to the next approver in the chain"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Rejecting an approval request sends the document back to Open status, allowing the original requester to make changes and send it for approval again.","source":{"title":"Approve or reject documents in workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-use-approval-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-70","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company wants approvals for several users to be routed to the same group of approvers as a unit. Which Business Central concept lets a consultant define such a collection of approvers for use in workflow responses?","options":["Workflow user groups","Security groups","Dimension combinations","Item categories"],"correct":[0],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Workflow user groups let you define a set of approvers and a sequence, which a workflow response can reference so requests route through that group.","source":{"title":"Set up approval workflows — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-set-up-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-71","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant works through a purchase-approval example on the Workflow page. Which element specifies WHICH action or trigger starts the workflow step, such as sending a purchase document for approval?","options":["The On Condition column","The Then Response column","The When Event column","The Enabled toggle"],"correct":[2],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The When Event entry identifies the triggering event (for example, an approval request is sent for a purchase document) that starts the workflow step; conditions filter it and responses define what happens next.","source":{"title":"Create approval workflows to connect tasks — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-how-to-create-workflows"}},{"id":"gen-72","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An organization wants approvers reminded about requests that have not been acted on within a set time. Which capability of workflow notifications addresses stale or overdue approval requests?","options":["The costing method on the item card","Overdue approval notifications sent to approvers","The additional reporting currency","The default dimension priority"],"correct":[1],"skill":1,"sub":"1.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Workflow notifications include reminders for overdue approval requests, alerting approvers (and administrators) when requests remain unactioned so they can be resolved.","source":{"title":"Setting up approval workflow notifications — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-setting-up-workflow-notifications"}},{"id":"gen-73","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is configuring a new Business Central company and must record the general ledger account that revenues and costs are posted to as unrealized when a payment discount is granted. Which page holds fields such as the payment discount, rounding, and default posting settings that apply across the whole general ledger?","options":["General Ledger Setup","General Posting Setup","General Journal Templates","Accounting Periods"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The General Ledger Setup page holds company-wide financial settings such as the local currency, address format, invoice rounding, and payment discount accounts that govern how the ledger behaves.","source":{"title":"Set up financial processes — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-setup-finance"}},{"id":"gen-74","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer's payment terms state that invoices are due one month after the invoice date. Which date formula should the consultant enter in the Due Date Calculation field of the payment terms code to achieve this?","options":["1D","CM","1M","30D+CM"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The date formula 1M adds one month to the document date, so the due date falls exactly one month after the invoice date.","source":{"title":"Set up payment terms — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-payment-terms"}},{"id":"gen-75","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants customers who pay early to receive a 2% discount if they pay within 14 days, while the invoice itself is due in 30 days. Which two fields on the Payment Terms card should be configured to enable this?","options":["Due Date Calculation and Calculate Pmt. Disc. on Cr. Memos","Max. No. of Days till Due Date and Discount %","Due Date Calculation and Realized VAT","Discount Date Calculation and Discount %"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Discount Date Calculation field sets the period within which an early payment qualifies, and the Discount % field sets the percentage granted, together defining the payment discount.","source":{"title":"Set up payment terms — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-payment-terms"}},{"id":"gen-76","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During implementation, a consultant needs to divide the fiscal year into 12 monthly periods so that reports and statistics can be generated by period. Which action on the Accounting Periods page creates these periods automatically?","options":["Close Year","Close Income Statement","Adjust Exchange Rates","Create Fiscal Year"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Create Fiscal Year action generates the accounting periods for a year based on a starting date, number of periods, and period length, marking the first period's New Fiscal Year field.","source":{"title":"Working with accounting periods and fiscal years — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-accounting-periods-and-fiscal-years"}},{"id":"gen-77","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After running the Close Year process for the fiscal year, what state are the accounting periods placed in, and what does this mean for posting?","options":["The periods are deleted and cannot be posted to again","The periods are marked as Closed but you can still post to them, though entries are flagged as posted to a closed period","The periods are locked so that no user, including administrators, can ever post to them","The periods are hidden from all reports until reopened"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Closing a fiscal year marks its periods as Closed and sets the Date Locked field, but you can still post to a closed year; such entries are marked as Prior-Year Entry and posted to a closed period.","source":{"title":"Working with accounting periods and fiscal years — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-accounting-periods-and-fiscal-years"}},{"id":"gen-78","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company based in the United States operates its accounts in USD but must also report consolidated figures to a parent company in EUR. Which Business Central feature lets the company store amounts in a second currency on every G/L entry for reporting purposes?","options":["Local Currency (LCY)","Additional Reporting Currency","Currency Exchange Rate Service","Payment Tolerance"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Additional Reporting Currency, set in General Ledger Setup, records amounts in a second currency on each G/L entry, enabling reporting in a currency other than the local currency.","source":{"title":"Currencies in Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-currencies"}},{"id":"gen-79","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is setting up a foreign currency and must ensure that Business Central can recalculate outstanding balances when exchange rates change. Where are the exchange rates that relate a foreign currency to the local currency entered?","options":["On the Currencies list only, in a single Exchange Rate field","In the General Ledger Setup under Local Currency","On the Currency Exchange Rates page for each currency, by effective date","On the customer and vendor cards individually"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Each currency has a Currency Exchange Rates page where you enter exchange rates by starting date, so Business Central can convert amounts and adjust balances as rates change over time.","source":{"title":"Currencies in Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-currencies"}},{"id":"gen-80","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A subscription business invoices a customer for a full year of service in advance but must recognize the revenue evenly across the 12 months. Which Business Central feature should the consultant configure to spread this income to the correct accounting periods?","options":["Payment terms with a discount","A deferral template","An additional reporting currency","A recurring general journal only"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Deferral templates let you automatically defer revenues or expenses to the periods in which they are earned or incurred, spreading the amount across the schedule rather than recognizing it all at once.","source":{"title":"Defer revenues and expenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-how-defer-revenue-expenses"}},{"id":"gen-81","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On a deferral template, which field determines how the total amount is distributed across the deferral periods, for example equally per period or based on the number of days in each period?","options":["Deferral Account","Calc. Method","Start Date","No. of Periods"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Calc. Method field on the deferral template controls how amounts are allocated, with options such as Straight-Line, Equal per Period, Days per Period, and User-Defined.","source":{"title":"Defer revenues and expenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-how-defer-revenue-expenses"}},{"id":"gen-82","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant assigns a payment terms code to a vendor card. When a purchase invoice is later created for that vendor, how does Business Central use the payment terms?","options":["It ignores the vendor's terms and always uses the General Ledger Setup default","It requires the user to manually type the due date on every document","It copies the payment terms code to the document and calculates the due date and any discount date accordingly","It applies the terms only after the invoice is posted"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Payment terms assigned on a customer or vendor card default onto their documents, where Business Central uses them to calculate the due date and any payment discount date automatically.","source":{"title":"Set up payment terms — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-payment-terms"}},{"id":"gen-83","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which statement best describes the role of the local currency (LCY) in a Business Central company?","options":["It is optional and only used when foreign transactions occur","It must be changed for each fiscal year","It is the same as the additional reporting currency","It is the base currency in which the company keeps its accounts, and all amounts are ultimately stored in LCY"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The local currency (LCY) is the company's base accounting currency; every transaction is recorded in LCY, and foreign-currency amounts are converted to LCY using exchange rates.","source":{"title":"Currencies in Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-currencies"}},{"id":"gen-84","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant follows the Set up financial processes guidance to prepare a company's finance area. Which of the following is a core financial setup task described there?","options":["Setting up the chart of accounts and posting groups","Configuring warehouse bin policies","Defining manufacturing routings","Creating item journal templates for production"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Setting up financial management includes establishing the chart of accounts, posting groups, payment terms and methods, currencies, and accounting periods so transactions post correctly.","source":{"title":"Set up financial processes — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-setup-finance"}},{"id":"gen-85","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A finance manager wants to prevent users from posting transactions into an earlier date range that has been reconciled. Which two fields in General Ledger Setup restrict the date range in which general postings are allowed?","options":["Allow Posting From and Allow Posting To","Starting Date and Ending Date","New Fiscal Year and Date Locked","Register Time and Pmt. Disc. Excl. VAT"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Allow Posting From and Allow Posting To fields in General Ledger Setup (or on a user's setup) define the range of dates in which posting is permitted, blocking entries outside that window.","source":{"title":"Set up financial processes — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-setup-finance"}},{"id":"gen-86","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs Business Central to automatically update the value of foreign-currency customer and vendor balances after month-end rate changes. Which process uses the currency exchange rates to revalue those outstanding entries?","options":["Close Income Statement","Adjust Exchange Rates","Create Fiscal Year","Suggest Vendor Payments"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Adjust Exchange Rates process recalculates the LCY value of foreign-currency balances using the latest exchange rates and posts the resulting unrealized gains or losses.","source":{"title":"Currencies in Business Central — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-currencies"}},{"id":"gen-87","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When posting a purchase invoice that includes a deferral, the deferral schedule can be reviewed and edited before posting. What does this schedule show?","options":["The bank accounts used for payment","The exchange rates for each currency","The approval users for the document","The G/L account and the amounts to be recognized in each future period"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The deferral schedule lists each period, its posting date, and the amount to be recognized, allowing you to review or adjust how the deferred amount is distributed before posting.","source":{"title":"Defer revenues and expenses — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-how-defer-revenue-expenses"}},{"id":"gen-88","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants a payment terms code where the entire balance is due at the end of the month following the invoice month. Which due date calculation formula achieves this?","options":["CM","1M+CM","1D+1M","1Y"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The formula 1M+CM adds one month to the document date and then moves to the end of that month (current month), so the due date is the last day of the month after the invoice month.","source":{"title":"Set up payment terms — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-payment-terms"}},{"id":"gen-89","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which of the following accurately describes the relationship between fiscal years and accounting periods in Business Central?","options":["A fiscal year must always contain exactly four accounting periods","Accounting periods and fiscal years are unrelated and set up independently","Accounting periods are the sub-divisions of a fiscal year, and the period whose New Fiscal Year field is enabled marks the start of a new year","Accounting periods can only be created after the year is closed"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Accounting periods subdivide a fiscal year; the period that has the New Fiscal Year field enabled defines where a new fiscal year begins, and Create Fiscal Year generates the periods within it.","source":{"title":"Working with accounting periods and fiscal years — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-accounting-periods-and-fiscal-years"}},{"id":"gen-90","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is completing the general financial setup and needs to specify the default number series used for journals, as well as rounding and discount posting behavior for the whole company. Which single page consolidates these company-wide financial defaults?","options":["General Ledger Setup","General Journal Templates","Chart of Accounts","Currencies"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The General Ledger Setup page centralizes company-wide financial defaults, including invoice rounding, payment discount handling, allowed posting dates, and local and reporting currencies.","source":{"title":"Set up financial processes — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-setup-finance"}},{"id":"gen-91","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant posts a sales invoice for a customer. Business Central must automatically determine which receivables G/L account is debited. Which posting group provides the receivables account used in this posting?","options":["The Customer Posting Group assigned to the customer","The General Business Posting Group on the customer","The VAT Business Posting Group on the customer","The Gen. Prod. Posting Group on the item"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Customer Posting Group defines balance-sheet accounts such as Receivables Account, and payment discount and rounding accounts, that Business Central uses when posting customer transactions.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-92","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When posting the revenue (income) portion of a sales line, Business Central selects the sales G/L account from the General Posting Setup. Which two fields form the key that the General Posting Setup uses to find that account?","options":["VAT Bus. Posting Group and VAT Prod. Posting Group","Customer Posting Group and Vendor Posting Group","Gen. Bus. Posting Group and Gen. Prod. Posting Group","Inventory Posting Group and Location Code"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"General Posting Setup is a matrix keyed by the combination of General Business Posting Group and General Product Posting Group, and it supplies the sales, purchase, COGS, and discount accounts.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-93","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs the correct VAT/sales tax G/L accounts to be selected automatically when posting an EU customer's domestic-rate item. Which setup determines the VAT payable and receivable accounts for that combination?","options":["General Posting Setup for the Gen. Bus./Gen. Prod. combination","Customer Posting Group for the customer","Inventory Posting Setup for the location","VAT Posting Setup for the VAT Bus./VAT Prod. Posting Group combination"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"VAT Posting Setup is a matrix keyed by VAT Business Posting Group and VAT Product Posting Group; it holds the VAT %, calculation type, and the sales and purchase VAT accounts.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-94","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During posting of an inventory item's cost, Business Central must find the inventory account on the balance sheet. Which posting setup provides that inventory account?","options":["Inventory Posting Setup, keyed by Inventory Posting Group and Location Code","General Posting Setup, keyed by the two general posting groups","Customer Posting Group for the sold-to customer","VAT Posting Setup for the item's VAT product group"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Inventory Posting Setup is keyed by Inventory Posting Group and Location Code, and it defines the inventory (and WIP) accounts used when inventory value is posted to the general ledger.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-95","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A functional consultant is asked to explain the difference between the two categories of posting groups in Business Central. How are specific posting groups distinguished from general posting groups?","options":["Specific posting groups apply only to sales, general posting groups only to purchases","General posting groups are mandatory, specific posting groups are optional in every scenario","Specific posting groups are used only for VAT, general posting groups only for inventory","Specific posting groups link master records (customers, vendors, items, banks) directly to balance-sheet accounts, while general posting groups combine to select income-statement accounts"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Specific posting groups (customer, vendor, bank, inventory, FA) tie a master record to particular balance-sheet accounts; general posting groups (business and product) are combined in the General Posting Setup to determine income-statement accounts.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-96","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer places a purchase, and the vendor invoice must post the payables balance automatically. Which posting group supplies the Payables Account used for the vendor?","options":["The Gen. Bus. Posting Group on the vendor","The VAT Bus. Posting Group on the vendor","The Vendor Posting Group assigned to the vendor","The General Posting Setup line for the purchase"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Vendor Posting Group defines the Payables Account plus payment discount, rounding, and interest accounts that Business Central uses when posting vendor transactions.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-97","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A new company code has been created and G/L accounts exist, but posting a sales order fails with a message that a General Posting Setup account is missing. What is the most likely cause?","options":["The Chart of Accounts has not been assigned a numbering series","The combination of Gen. Bus. Posting Group and Gen. Prod. Posting Group used on the document has no line, or an empty account field, in the General Posting Setup","The customer has no Customer Posting Group","The item has no Inventory Posting Group"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"General Posting Setup must contain a line for each business/product posting group combination in use, with the relevant income-statement accounts filled in; a missing line or blank account stops posting.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-98","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In the Chart of Accounts, an account is defined with a Direct Posting setting. What does clearing (disabling) Direct Posting on a G/L account accomplish?","options":["It hides the account from financial reports","It converts the account into a heading with no balance","It deletes any existing ledger entries on the account","It prevents users from posting directly to the account in journals, so it receives entries only from automated postings or subledgers"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Clearing Direct Posting blocks manual journal entries to the account; the account can still receive amounts from processes and posting-setup-driven postings, which protects control accounts.","source":{"title":"Understanding the Chart of Accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-chart-of-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-99","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants each G/L account to map to a line on the balance sheet or income statement for financial reporting. Which feature on the G/L account is used to establish this mapping?","options":["The Account Category and Account Subcategory fields","The Gen. Posting Type field","The Direct Posting toggle","The Reconciliation Account checkbox"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Account Category and Subcategory group G/L accounts (for example as Assets, Liabilities, Income, or Cost of Goods Sold) so that financial reports can be generated based on the categories.","source":{"title":"Understand the general ledger and Chart of Accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-general-ledger"}},{"id":"gen-100","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On a G/L account card used for sales and purchases, the Gen. Posting Type field is set. Why is setting Gen. Posting Type (Sale or Purchase) on such accounts important?","options":["It defines the account's currency for reporting","It, together with the general and VAT posting groups on the account, lets the system verify and calculate VAT correctly when amounts post to the account","It blocks direct posting to the account automatically","It determines the number series for the account"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Gen. Posting Type (Sale/Purchase) combined with the general business/product and VAT posting groups on the account enables Business Central to apply the correct VAT posting setup when transactions hit the account.","source":{"title":"Understanding the Chart of Accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-chart-of-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-101","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is configuring the General Posting Setup and wants sales-related discounts to post to a dedicated account. Which account is populated in the General Posting Setup for this purpose?","options":["Receivables Account","Inventory Account","Purch. VAT Account","Sales Line Disc. Account (and Sales Inv. Disc. Account)"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The General Posting Setup line for a business/product group combination includes sales and purchase accounts plus dedicated discount accounts such as Sales Line Disc. Account and Sales Inv. Disc. Account.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-102","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A retailer sells the same item from both a warehouse location and a store location and wants inventory value tracked to different G/L accounts per location. How does Business Central support this automatic account selection?","options":["By assigning a different Customer Posting Group per location","By using a separate VAT Posting Setup per location","By creating Inventory Posting Setup lines that combine the item's Inventory Posting Group with each Location Code","By setting Direct Posting differently on each inventory account"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Because Inventory Posting Setup is keyed by Inventory Posting Group and Location Code, the same item can post to different inventory accounts depending on the location.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-103","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Business Central allows assigning multiple posting groups to a single customer or vendor so a different balance-sheet account can be chosen at posting time. What must be enabled for a user to select an alternative posting group on a document?","options":["Direct Posting must be cleared on the receivables account","The Allow Multiple Posting Groups setting must be enabled and the permitted groups defined for that customer or vendor","A separate number series must be created for each posting group","The account category must be set to Receivables"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Multiple posting groups let you change the customer or vendor posting group on a document; this requires enabling the multiple-posting-groups feature and specifying which groups are allowed for the master record.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-104","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is building an income statement in financial reporting and wants rows to summarize amounts from groups of accounts rather than individual accounts. Which mechanism best supports maintainable rows that survive changes to the chart of accounts?","options":["Row definitions based on account categories/subcategories rather than hard-coded account numbers","A separate posting group per report row","Blocking direct posting on every summary account","A dedicated VAT posting setup per row"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Financial reports can be built from account categories, so rows summarize categorized accounts; this keeps the Balance Sheet and Income Statement stable when accounts are added or changed.","source":{"title":"Build financial reports using financial data and account categories — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bi-how-work-account-schedule"}},{"id":"gen-105","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A financial report is being defined. Which two components together determine what appears in the report matrix?","options":["Posting groups and number series","Customer posting groups and vendor posting groups","Inventory posting setup and general posting setup","Row definitions and column definitions"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Financial reports combine a row definition (what accounts/categories are shown) with a column definition (periods, net change, budget comparisons) to produce the report output.","source":{"title":"Build financial reports using financial data and account categories — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bi-how-work-account-schedule"}},{"id":"gen-106","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant adds a new G/L account of type Heading and another of type Total to the chart of accounts. What is the purpose of these account types?","options":["They store posted ledger entries like a posting account","They determine which VAT posting setup is used","They structure and subtotal the chart of accounts for readability and totaling, without receiving direct postings","They replace the need for account categories"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Heading, Total, Begin-Total, and End-Total account types organize and subtotal the chart of accounts; only Posting-type accounts receive transaction entries.","source":{"title":"Understanding the Chart of Accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-chart-of-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-107","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When a sales invoice with an inventory item is posted, several posting groups act together. Which statement correctly describes how the accounts are selected?","options":["All accounts come solely from the Customer Posting Group","The Customer Posting Group gives the receivables account, the General Posting Setup gives the sales and COGS accounts, the VAT Posting Setup gives the VAT account, and the Inventory Posting Setup gives the inventory account","The General Posting Setup provides the receivables and VAT accounts, and the Customer Posting Group provides the sales account","Only the Inventory Posting Setup and VAT Posting Setup are involved"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A single posted transaction draws on several posting groups at once: specific groups (customer, inventory) supply balance-sheet accounts while the general and VAT posting setups supply income-statement and VAT accounts.","source":{"title":"Posting group setup — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-posting-groups"}},{"id":"gen-108","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The general ledger is described as the central repository of financial data in Business Central. Which statement best reflects the relationship between the Chart of Accounts and the general ledger?","options":["The Chart of Accounts is a report generated from posted G/L entries","The general ledger stores only VAT entries, while the Chart of Accounts stores everything else","The Chart of Accounts and general ledger are unrelated modules","The Chart of Accounts lists the G/L accounts to which transactions post, and General Ledger Setup plus posting groups control how those postings occur"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Chart of Accounts defines the G/L accounts used for posting; General Ledger Setup and the posting group configuration govern how transactions are routed to those accounts.","source":{"title":"Understand the general ledger and Chart of Accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-general-ledger"}},{"id":"gen-109","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is configuring the General Journal for a new Business Central company. The client wants every journal batch used for month-end accruals to automatically assign document numbers from a dedicated series, while a separate cash batch uses its own series. At which level should the consultant assign the number series so each batch can draw from a different series?","options":["On the journal template only, so all batches inherit one shared series","On the General Ledger Setup page as a single global journal series","On the No. Series field of each individual journal batch","On each G/L account card that the journal will post to"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"In general journals the number series is set on the journal batch (in the No. Series field), so different batches under the same template can use different series for document numbering.","source":{"title":"Working with general journals — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"gen-110","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A client posts rent and other fixed monthly amounts through a recurring general journal. They want the same journal lines to remain in the batch after posting so they can be reused next month without re-entering them. Which journal feature is designed for this requirement?","options":["A standard general journal template with manual re-entry each period","A recurring general journal with a recurring method and recurring frequency","A payment journal batch with the Suggest Vendor Payments batch job","A cash receipt journal with automatic application"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Recurring general journals keep the lines after posting and use a recurring method and a recurring frequency (a date formula) to control how amounts and dates behave for the next period.","source":{"title":"Working with general journals — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"gen-111","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During setup, a functional consultant notices that the same set of frequently used general journal lines needs to be available on demand but should NOT post automatically on a schedule. Which capability lets a user save a filled-in journal and re-open it later as a starting point?","options":["Save the batch as a standard general journal and retrieve it with Get Standard Journals","Convert the batch into a recurring journal with a blank recurring frequency","Export the lines to Excel and re-import them each time","Enable Force Doc. Balance on the journal template"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A standard general journal stores a set of journal lines that can be reused; users save them and later retrieve them with the Get Standard Journals action, without any scheduled posting.","source":{"title":"Working with general journals — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"gen-112","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A general journal batch already contains many lines whose document numbers are now out of sequence after several deletions. The consultant wants Business Central to reassign consecutive numbers based on the batch's number series before posting. Which action accomplishes this?","options":["Delete and re-create the batch to reset numbering","Change the number series on the journal template","Choose the Renumber Document Numbers action on the journal","Post the journal and let it renumber automatically"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Renumber Document Numbers action reassigns document numbers on the journal lines so they are consecutive, using the batch's number series, which helps avoid posting errors from gaps.","source":{"title":"Working with general journals — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"gen-113","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is explaining the relationship between journal templates and journal batches to a client. Which statement correctly describes their roles in Business Central?","options":["Batches define the page and posting behavior, while templates are just named filters under a batch","Templates and batches are interchangeable and only one is ever required","Batches must be created before any template can be defined","Templates define the type and default page/behavior, while batches are named subsets used to separate work and numbering"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A journal template defines the journal type, page, and defaults; batches are named instances under a template used to segregate work (for example by user or purpose) and can carry their own number series.","source":{"title":"Working with general journals — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-work-general-journals"}},{"id":"gen-114","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When creating a new bank account card in Business Central, which setup on the card determines the general ledger accounts that bank transactions post to?","options":["The Bank Account Posting Group assigned on the bank account card","The Gen. Bus. Posting Group only","The Customer Posting Group referenced by the bank","The number series assigned to the bank account"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Each bank account is linked to a Bank Account Posting Group, which specifies the G/L account that bank transactions for that account post to.","source":{"title":"Set up bank accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bank-how-setup-bank-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-115","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A client is going live and needs to record the starting balance for a newly created bank account so it agrees with the last bank statement. What is the recommended way to enter this opening balance in Business Central?","options":["Type the balance directly into the Balance field on the bank account card","Post the opening balance through a general journal (or cash receipt journal) line to the bank account","Enter it in the Bank Account Posting Group setup","Import it automatically when the bank account card is created"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Bank account balances are the result of posted entries, so an opening balance is entered by posting a journal line (for example a general or cash receipt journal) to the bank account rather than typed on the card.","source":{"title":"Set up bank accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bank-how-setup-bank-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-116","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs a bank account to support importing electronic bank statement files and exporting payment files for a specific bank. Which setup on the bank account card enables Business Central to handle these file formats?","options":["Assign a Bank Account Posting Group that matches the bank","Set the Currency Code to the bank's currency","Configure the Bank Statement Import Format and Payment Export Format fields","Enable Direct Debit Mandate on the bank account"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The import and export of bank files is controlled by the bank statement import format and the payment export format defined on the bank account card, often provided through data exchange definitions or bank connectivity extensions.","source":{"title":"Set up bank accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bank-how-setup-bank-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-117","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"At month-end, a client wants to compare the transactions recorded on a bank account in Business Central against the entries on the bank's statement and match them, without necessarily using imported payment data to close open invoices. Which tool is intended for this reconciliation?","options":["The Payment Reconciliation Journal only","The Cash Receipt Journal","The Suggest Vendor Payments batch job","The Bank Account Reconciliation"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Bank Account Reconciliation compares bank account ledger entries with bank statement lines and matches them, which is the standard tool for reconciling a bank account to its statement.","source":{"title":"Manage bank accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bank-manage-bank-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-118","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A client wants to reconcile the bank and, in the same process, automatically apply incoming and outgoing payments to open customer and vendor ledger entries based on an imported bank statement. Which journal best supports this combined workflow?","options":["The Payment Reconciliation Journal","The standard General Journal","The Recurring General Journal","The Fixed Asset G/L Journal"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Payment Reconciliation Journal imports bank statement data, then applies payments to open customer and vendor entries and reconciles the bank account in one step.","source":{"title":"Manage bank accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bank-manage-bank-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-119","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During a bank reconciliation, several statement lines represent bank charges and interest that have no corresponding entry yet in Business Central. What is the appropriate way to handle these lines so the reconciliation can be completed?","options":["Delete the statement lines because they have no match","Force-match them to unrelated customer entries","Post them from within the reconciliation as new entries (for example to a G/L charges account)","Change the bank account posting group to absorb the difference"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Statement lines with no existing ledger entry, such as bank charges or interest, can be posted directly from the reconciliation to the appropriate G/L account so the bank balance reconciles.","source":{"title":"Manage bank accounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/bank-manage-bank-accounts"}},{"id":"gen-120","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer sends a single payment that covers three separate open invoices. In the cash receipt journal, how should the consultant record the receipt so it clears all three invoices correctly?","options":["Create three separate journal lines, one per invoice, and post them individually only","Enter one line for the customer and use Apply Entries to distribute the amount across the three open invoices","Post the payment to a G/L suspense account and adjust later","Reduce each invoice manually on the posted sales invoice pages"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"In the cash receipt journal you enter the payment for the customer and use Apply Entries to select and apply the amount against multiple open customer ledger entries before posting.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with the cash receipt journal — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"gen-121","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After posting a customer payment in the cash receipt journal, the accountant realizes the payment was applied to the wrong invoice. Which action lets them correct the application without reversing the payment posting itself?","options":["Delete the posted customer ledger entry","Re-post the same payment to offset the error","Edit the Applies-to Doc. No. on the posted entry directly","Use Unapply Entries on the customer ledger entry, then re-apply to the correct invoice"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Unapply Entries function reverses an incorrect application on the customer ledger entry, after which the payment can be re-applied to the correct open invoice.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with the cash receipt journal — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"gen-122","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant sets the Applies-to ID on selected customer ledger entries while entering a payment in the cash receipt journal. What is the purpose of setting the Applies-to ID?","options":["It marks which open entries the payment will be applied to when posted","It changes the customer's posting group for the transaction","It assigns a new document number series to the journal","It blocks the customer from further postings"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Setting the Applies-to ID flags the specific open customer ledger entries that the payment should settle, so those entries are closed when the journal is posted.","source":{"title":"Reconcile customer payments with the cash receipt journal — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/receivables-how-apply-sales-transactions-manually"}},{"id":"gen-123","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An accounts payable clerk needs to pay all vendor invoices that are due within the next week. In the payment journal, which action populates the journal with proposed vendor payments based on due dates and available payment discounts?","options":["Get Standard Journals","Suggest Vendor Payments","Renumber Document Numbers","Apply Entries"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Suggest Vendor Payments batch job fills the payment journal with lines for open vendor entries based on criteria such as due date and payment discount date.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage payments to vendors — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/payables-make-payments"}},{"id":"gen-124","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In the payment journal, a client wants each vendor payment to draw a check number and print computer checks before posting. Which combination of settings on the payment journal line supports printing checks?","options":["Set Bal. Account Type to Vendor and print from the vendor card","Set the Bank Payment Type to Computer Check and use a bank Bal. Account, then Print Check","Set the Document Type to Invoice and post directly","Leave the Bal. Account blank and print from G/L Setup"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"To print checks, the payment journal line uses a bank balancing account and the Bank Payment Type set to Computer Check, after which the Print Check action produces the check before posting.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage payments to vendors — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/payables-make-payments"}},{"id":"gen-125","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A vendor was overpaid and the client wants to record the refund the vendor returns. Which approach fits the payments-to-vendors process in Business Central?","options":["Delete the original posted payment entry","Increase the next invoice amount to offset the refund","Change the vendor posting group to reverse the balance","Post a refund document type in the payment journal and apply it to the related vendor entry"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A vendor refund is recorded with the Refund document type in the payment journal and applied to the relevant vendor ledger entry, keeping the vendor balance accurate without deleting posted entries.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage payments to vendors — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/payables-make-payments"}},{"id":"gen-126","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When suggesting vendor payments, a consultant wants Business Central to combine multiple open entries for the same vendor into a single payment line and document number. Which option on the Suggest Vendor Payments request page controls this?","options":["Set the Posting Date to a future period","Clear the Bal. Account No. field","Set Bank Payment Type to Manual Check","Enable Summarize per Vendor"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Summarize per Vendor option on the Suggest Vendor Payments batch job groups a vendor's open entries into one combined payment line rather than a separate line per invoice.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage payments to vendors — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/payables-make-payments"}},{"id":"gen-127","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is configuring fixed assets for a new company and wants to follow Microsoft's recommended sequence. Which task must be completed before assets can have depreciation calculated and posted?","options":["Post the first disposal entry so the system establishes a gain/loss account","Set up at least one depreciation book and assign it to the fixed assets","Run the Calculate Depreciation batch job once with no lines","Create a fixed asset G/L journal template named DEFAULT"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Depreciation books are the required backbone of the FA module; you must create at least one depreciation book and attach it to each asset before any depreciation can be calculated or posted.","source":{"title":"Set up fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-setup"}},{"id":"gen-128","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In Business Central, what is the primary purpose of a fixed asset depreciation book?","options":["It stores the vendor invoice numbers used to acquire each asset","It defines the user permissions required to post FA transactions","It holds the settings and ledger entries that control how an asset is valued and depreciated","It links each asset to a specific bank account for payments"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A depreciation book contains the depreciation settings (method, dates, posting rules) and accumulates the FA ledger entries that determine how an asset is valued over its life.","source":{"title":"Set Up FA Depreciation — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-depreciation"}},{"id":"gen-129","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company must keep one set of asset values for financial reporting and a separate set for tax reporting. How should this be configured in Business Central?","options":["Create two separate fixed asset cards for each physical asset","Set up two depreciation books and assign both to the assets","Post depreciation twice per period into the same book","Use two different FA posting groups on a single depreciation book"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Multiple depreciation books let a company depreciate the same asset differently for different purposes, such as financial versus tax reporting, by assigning more than one book to each asset.","source":{"title":"Set Up FA Depreciation — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-depreciation"}},{"id":"gen-130","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which setup determines the general ledger accounts that fixed asset acquisition, depreciation, and disposal transactions post to?","options":["FA posting groups","FA classes","FA locations","Global dimensions"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"FA posting groups map fixed asset transaction types (acquisition cost, depreciation, disposal, gains/losses) to the specific G/L accounts used when posting.","source":{"title":"Set Up General Fixed Assets Information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-131","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to group assets for reporting into categories such as Tangible and Intangible, and then more granularly into Buildings and Vehicles. Which two FA setup features support this?","options":["Depreciation books and FA journal batches","FA posting groups and number series","FA classes and FA subclasses","Global dimensions and shortcut dimensions"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"FA classes provide a high-level grouping (for example Tangible/Intangible) and FA subclasses provide a more detailed grouping within a class, both used for classification and reporting.","source":{"title":"Set Up General Fixed Assets Information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-132","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which depreciation method reduces an asset's value by the same amount in each depreciation period across its useful life?","options":["Declining-Balance 1","Straight-Line","Declining-Balance 2","Half-Year Convention"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Straight-Line method spreads the depreciable cost evenly, depreciating the asset by an equal amount in each period over its useful life.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"gen-133","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A finance manager wants assets to depreciate faster in the early years, applying a fixed percentage to the declining book value each period. Which depreciation method fits this requirement?","options":["Straight-Line","Manual","Declining-Balance","User-Defined"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Declining-Balance methods apply a fixed percentage to the remaining book value each period, producing larger depreciation amounts early in the asset's life and smaller amounts later.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"gen-134","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant selects the DB1/SL depreciation method for an asset. What behavior does this combined method produce?","options":["It depreciates using both methods and posts the higher of the two amounts each period","It depreciates using both methods and posts the lower of the two amounts each period","It requires the user to manually enter each period's amount","It ignores the useful life and depreciates fully in the first year"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"DB1/SL calculates depreciation with both Declining-Balance 1 and Straight-Line each period and uses the larger amount, switching to straight-line once it yields the higher figure.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"gen-135","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An asset should not depreciate on a calculated schedule; instead the accountant will enter each depreciation amount manually as needed. Which depreciation method should be assigned in the depreciation book?","options":["Straight-Line","Declining-Balance 1","Half-Year Convention","Manual"],"correct":[3],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Manual method causes Business Central to calculate no depreciation, so the accountant enters depreciation amounts manually in the FA journal whenever required.","source":{"title":"Depreciation methods for fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-depreciation-methods"}},{"id":"gen-136","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During initial FA setup, which page is used to specify the default depreciation book and the number series for fixed assets and their journals?","options":["General Ledger Setup","Fixed Asset Setup","FA Posting Groups","Inventory Setup"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Fixed Asset Setup page holds general FA information such as the default depreciation book and the number series used for fixed assets and FA journals.","source":{"title":"Set Up General Fixed Assets Information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-137","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to create fixed asset journals for posting acquisitions and depreciation. What must be set up so these journals function correctly?","options":["Bank account reconciliation settings","FA journal templates and batches","Payment terms and payment methods","Customer and vendor posting groups"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"As part of general FA setup, you create FA journal templates and batches (including the FA G/L journal and FA journal) so that FA transactions can be entered and posted.","source":{"title":"Set Up General Fixed Assets Information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-138","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Where in Business Central do you specify the depreciation method, depreciation starting date, and number of depreciation years or ending date for a specific asset?","options":["On the FA posting group card","On the FA class card","On the depreciation book line of the fixed asset card","On the General Ledger Setup page"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Each asset's depreciation book lines (on the fixed asset card) hold the depreciation method, starting date, and either the number of depreciation years or the depreciation ending date.","source":{"title":"Set Up FA Depreciation — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-depreciation"}},{"id":"gen-139","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"What is the correct relationship between a fixed asset card and depreciation books in Business Central?","options":["Each fixed asset can be assigned to one or more depreciation books","Each depreciation book can contain only one fixed asset","A fixed asset cannot be linked to any depreciation book until it is disposed","Depreciation books are assigned to FA classes, not to individual assets"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A single fixed asset can be assigned to one or several depreciation books, which enables parallel valuation for purposes such as financial and tax reporting.","source":{"title":"Set Up FA Depreciation — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-depreciation"}},{"id":"gen-140","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company registers a new machine and wants to record its acquisition. Which lifecycle action correctly reflects how fixed assets are managed in Business Central?","options":["The asset is created directly as a posted disposal entry","An asset card is created, then acquisition cost is posted, followed by depreciation over its life, and finally disposal","Assets must be fully depreciated before an acquisition cost can be posted","Depreciation is posted before the acquisition cost to establish the book value"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The FA lifecycle is: create the asset card, post the acquisition cost, depreciate the asset over its useful life, and eventually dispose of or retire it.","source":{"title":"Manage fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-manage"}},{"id":"gen-141","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to track insurance coverage and maintenance costs for company assets. Which statement about these FA capabilities is correct?","options":["Insurance and maintenance can only be recorded outside Business Central","Business Central supports registering insurance policies and recording maintenance for fixed assets","Maintenance can be tracked only for assets using the Manual depreciation method","Insurance tracking replaces the need for a depreciation book"],"correct":[1],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"As part of managing fixed assets, Business Central lets you set up insurance to monitor whether assets are adequately covered and record maintenance costs against assets.","source":{"title":"Manage fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-manage"}},{"id":"gen-142","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which optional fixed asset setup lets a consultant record where assets are physically located and who is responsible for them?","options":["FA posting groups","Depreciation books","FA locations","Number series"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"FA locations are an optional setup used to organize assets by physical location and can be combined with responsible employees to track custody of assets.","source":{"title":"Set Up General Fixed Assets Information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-143","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When setting up a fixed asset, which value is used together with cost to determine the depreciable base, representing the estimated residual value at the end of the asset's life?","options":["Salvage value","Acquisition cost","Book value","Write-down amount"],"correct":[0],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Salvage value is the estimated residual value at the end of an asset's useful life; the depreciable base is the acquisition cost reduced by the salvage value.","source":{"title":"Set Up FA Depreciation — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-setup-depreciation"}},{"id":"gen-144","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant reviews the required versus optional fixed asset setup tasks. Which of the following is a required setup rather than an optional one?","options":["Setting up insurance policies for assets","Setting up FA locations for physical tracking","Setting up depreciation books and FA posting groups","Setting up maintenance registration for assets"],"correct":[2],"skill":2,"sub":"2.4","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Depreciation books and FA posting groups are required to calculate and post FA transactions, whereas insurance, maintenance, and FA locations are optional enhancements.","source":{"title":"Set up fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-setup"}},{"id":"gen-145","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A functional consultant is configuring a new item that is a physical good tracked in inventory, with quantities that must be increased by purchases and decreased by sales. Which item Type should be selected on the item card?","options":["Service","Non-Inventory","Resource","Inventory"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Inventory item type is used for physical goods whose quantity is tracked, with item ledger entries created and inventory increased/decreased by transactions. Non-Inventory and Service types are not tracked in inventory quantity.","source":{"title":"Register new items — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-register-new-items"}},{"id":"gen-146","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"During implementation, a client wants every new item card to default to a specific costing method unless changed manually. Where does a consultant define the value that new items inherit as their costing method?","options":["The Default Costing Method field on the Inventory Setup page","The Costing Method field on each Item Category card","The General Ledger Setup page","The Inventory Posting Setup page"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Inventory Setup page contains a Default Costing Method field that is applied to new item cards, saving the user from setting it manually on every item. It can still be overridden per item.","source":{"title":"Set up general inventory information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-147","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A distributor sells identical, high-volume screws where each unit is interchangeable and management wants the cost of goods sold to reflect the oldest purchases first. Which costing method best fits this requirement?","options":["Specific","Standard","LIFO","FIFO"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"FIFO (First-In, First-Out) assumes the first items received are the first sold, so cost of goods sold uses the oldest acquisition costs. It suits interchangeable, high-volume goods.","source":{"title":"Design details - Inventory costing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-inventory-costing"}},{"id":"gen-148","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A manufacturer wants each item valued at a predetermined cost, with any difference between that cost and the actual purchase cost posted as a variance. Which costing method should be assigned?","options":["Standard","Average","FIFO","Specific"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Standard costing method values inventory at a predetermined standard cost; differences between standard and actual cost are posted as variances. It is common in manufacturing.","source":{"title":"Design details - Inventory costing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-inventory-costing"}},{"id":"gen-149","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A jewelry retailer must track and value each individual serialized item by its own actual acquisition cost. Which costing method is designed for this scenario?","options":["Average","FIFO","Specific","Standard"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Specific costing method values each unit by its own specific cost, typically used with serial-number tracking for unique or high-value items such as jewelry.","source":{"title":"Design details - Inventory costing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-inventory-costing"}},{"id":"gen-150","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant explains how the Average costing method calculates the unit cost of an item in Business Central. Which statement is correct?","options":["It uses the cost of the most recently received units","It uses a fixed budgeted cost set on the item card","It calculates a weighted average cost of the remaining inventory over an average cost period","It uses the cost of the earliest received units"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Average costing values items at a weighted average unit cost, recalculated per the defined average cost period (and optionally by variant/location). It does not track oldest or newest layers.","source":{"title":"Design details - Inventory costing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-inventory-costing"}},{"id":"gen-151","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A warehouse stocks the same item at three locations and needs to define a distinct reordering policy and replenishment settings per location. Which inventory feature should the consultant configure?","options":["Item variants","Stockkeeping units (SKUs)","Item categories","Item attributes"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Stockkeeping units let you store item information such as reordering policy and replenishment per location and/or variant, overriding the item card defaults for that location.","source":{"title":"Set up stockkeeping units — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-to-set-up-stockkeeping-units"}},{"id":"gen-152","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which prerequisite must be satisfied before stockkeeping units can be created for an item in Business Central?","options":["The item must use the Standard costing method","The item must be blocked from sales","A dedicated number series must exist for SKUs","Location Mandatory or variants/locations must be in use so SKUs can be defined per location or variant"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"SKUs represent an item at a specific location and/or variant, so locations (and optionally variants) must be set up to create meaningful stockkeeping units.","source":{"title":"Set up stockkeeping units — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-to-set-up-stockkeeping-units"}},{"id":"gen-153","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to represent the same T-shirt item in several colors, each sharing the same item number but distinguishable in inventory. Which item feature accomplishes this?","options":["Item categories","Item attributes","Item variants","Units of measure"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Item variants let a single item be tracked as different variations (for example colors or sizes) under one item number, with inventory kept per variant.","source":{"title":"Register new items — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-register-new-items"}},{"id":"gen-154","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An item is purchased in pallets but sold in individual pieces. Which item setup allows both purchasing and selling in different quantities of the same item?","options":["Item variants","Units of measure with a base unit and conversions","Item attributes","Stockkeeping units"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Units of measure define a base unit and additional units with quantity-per conversions, so an item can be purchased, stored, and sold in different units such as PALLET and PCS.","source":{"title":"Setting up inventory — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-setup-inventory"}},{"id":"gen-155","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to classify items into a hierarchy (for example Furniture > Chairs) so that items inherit shared attributes and can be grouped for reporting. Which feature should be used?","options":["Item categories","Item variants","Stockkeeping units","Posting groups"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Item categories organize items in a hierarchy and can carry default attributes that assigned items inherit, supporting grouping and reporting.","source":{"title":"Register new items — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-register-new-items"}},{"id":"gen-156","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to be able to filter and find items by searchable characteristics such as color, size, or material without changing the item number. Which feature meets this need?","options":["Units of measure","Item variants","Costing methods","Item attributes"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Item attributes add searchable characteristics (such as color or material) to items, letting users filter and locate items by those values.","source":{"title":"Register new items — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-register-new-items"}},{"id":"gen-157","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On the Inventory Setup page, which setting forces users to specify a location code on inventory documents and journal lines?","options":["Automatic Cost Posting","Location Mandatory","Expected Cost Posting to G/L","Prevent Negative Inventory"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Location Mandatory toggle on the Inventory Setup page requires a location code on item transactions, which is a prerequisite for multi-location inventory and SKUs.","source":{"title":"Set up general inventory information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-158","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A client wants inventory value changes in the item ledger to be posted to the general ledger automatically as transactions are posted, rather than run separately later. Which Inventory Setup field should be enabled?","options":["Automatic Cost Posting","Location Mandatory","Default Costing Method","Skip Prompt for Affected Lines"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Automatic Cost Posting on the Inventory Setup page posts inventory-related costs to the general ledger automatically when transactions post, instead of relying on the Post Inventory Cost to G/L batch job.","source":{"title":"Set up general inventory information — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-setup-general"}},{"id":"gen-159","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A newly created stockkeeping unit does not display a costing method field for editing. Why does the SKU inherit its costing method rather than allow a new one?","options":["SKUs never track cost","The costing method is defined on the item card and applies to all its stockkeeping units","Costing methods are set only on locations","The SKU must first be posted before costing appears"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The costing method is an item-level property; a stockkeeping unit represents that item at a location/variant and inherits the item's costing method rather than defining its own.","source":{"title":"Set up stockkeeping units — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-to-set-up-stockkeeping-units"}},{"id":"gen-160","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is asked which costing method assumes the most recently acquired items are sold first, so cost of goods sold reflects the latest purchase costs. Which method is this?","options":["FIFO","Average","LIFO","Specific"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"LIFO (Last-In, First-Out) assumes the most recently received items are sold first, so cost of goods sold uses the newest acquisition costs.","source":{"title":"Design details - Inventory costing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/design-details-inventory-costing"}},{"id":"gen-161","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When setting up inventory in a new company, which sequence reflects the recommended dependency of the core inventory elements?","options":["Create items first, then define locations and general inventory setup","Configure general inventory setup and locations, then create items, then optionally create SKUs","Create SKUs first, then items, then locations","Define costing methods per location before any inventory setup"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Setting up inventory starts with general inventory setup and locations, followed by items (with UoM, categories, variants), and finally stockkeeping units where needed per location/variant.","source":{"title":"Setting up inventory — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-setup-inventory"}},{"id":"gen-162","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant creates an item that represents labor or a non-tracked offering such as installation, which should not maintain any inventory quantity. Which item type is appropriate?","options":["Inventory","Variant","Standard","Service"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Service item type is used for items like labor that are not physically stocked, so no inventory quantity is maintained for them.","source":{"title":"Register new items — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-register-new-items"}},{"id":"gen-163","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A functional consultant wants new customer cards to be created quickly with common defaults such as the general business posting group, payment terms, and country/region already filled in. Which Business Central feature should be configured to achieve this?","options":["Customer templates","Shortcut dimension 1","A recurring general journal batch","A stockkeeping unit"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Customer (configuration) templates let you predefine field values that are copied onto new customer cards, so common data such as posting groups and payment terms is filled in automatically.","source":{"title":"Register new customers by creating a Customer Card — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-register-new-customers"}},{"id":"gen-164","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On a customer card, which field determines how much a customer is allowed to owe before Business Central warns you when you post additional sales documents?","options":["Balance (LCY)","Credit Limit (LCY)","Payment Terms Code","Blocked"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Credit Limit (LCY) field sets the maximum balance a customer may owe; exceeding it triggers a credit-limit warning when you create or post sales documents.","source":{"title":"Register new customers by creating a Customer Card — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-register-new-customers"}},{"id":"gen-165","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to prevent any new sales orders or shipments from being created for a customer who is under review, while still allowing existing invoices to be paid. Which customer card setting should be used?","options":["Set the Credit Limit (LCY) to 0","Remove the Salesperson Code","Set the Blocked field to Ship","Clear the Gen. Bus. Posting Group"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Setting the Blocked field to Ship stops new orders and shipments for the customer while still permitting invoicing and payment application; All would block everything.","source":{"title":"Register new customers by creating a Customer Card — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-register-new-customers"}},{"id":"gen-166","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which customer card field assigns the employee who is responsible for the customer relationship and can be used to filter reports and opportunities?","options":["Responsibility Center","Contact Code","Territory Code","Salesperson Code"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Salesperson Code links a salesperson to the customer, driving default assignment on documents and enabling salesperson-based reporting and opportunity tracking.","source":{"title":"Register new customers by creating a Customer Card — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-register-new-customers"}},{"id":"gen-167","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When registering a new vendor, a consultant wants payments to be sent to a bank account and address that differ from the vendor's main ordering address. Which vendor setup supports this?","options":["Remit-to addresses","Ship-to addresses","Order addresses only","Dimension defaults"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Remit-to addresses on the vendor let you record alternate addresses used for sending payments, separate from the vendor's primary buy-from address.","source":{"title":"Register a new vendor — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-register-new-vendors"}},{"id":"gen-168","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is creating many vendors that share the same currency, payment method, and posting groups. What is the most efficient way to apply these common values to each new vendor card?","options":["Enter the values manually on each card","Use a vendor template when creating the vendors","Create a configuration package after posting","Set the values in General Ledger Setup"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Vendor templates predefine field values such as currency, payment method, and posting groups so they are automatically applied to each new vendor card.","source":{"title":"Register a new vendor — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-register-new-vendors"}},{"id":"gen-169","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In Business Central's newer pricing experience, sales and purchase special prices and discounts are maintained primarily through which structure?","options":["Item journal lines","General posting setup","Price lists","Analysis views"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The new pricing experience centralizes special prices and discounts in price lists, which can apply to customers, vendors, groups, or all, replacing the older separate price/discount tables.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"gen-170","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"What is the key difference between a line discount and an invoice discount in Business Central?","options":["A line discount applies to a specific item or line, while an invoice discount applies to the whole document based on the total amount","A line discount is always a fixed amount, while an invoice discount is always a percentage","A line discount posts to inventory, while an invoice discount posts to fixed assets","A line discount requires approval, while an invoice discount does not"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Line discounts reduce the price on individual document lines (typically by item/quantity), whereas invoice discounts are calculated on the total document amount once it reaches a defined threshold.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"gen-171","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer should automatically receive an invoice discount once their order total reaches DKK 5,000. Which setup makes this happen when the sales document is created?","options":["A sales line discount on each item","A customer invoice discount code with a minimum amount and discount percentage","A payment discount in the payment terms","A price list line for the item"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"You assign an invoice discount code to the customer and define minimum-amount thresholds with percentages; when the document total reaches the threshold, the invoice discount is calculated automatically.","source":{"title":"Record special sales prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-record-sales-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-172","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When multiple sales prices could apply to a line, how does Business Central decide which unit price to use?","options":["It always uses the price on the item card","It uses the most recently created price line","It applies the lowest permissible price (best price) for the customer and conditions","It prompts the user to pick a price manually"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central uses best-price calculation, selecting the lowest price and highest line discount among all applicable price agreements for the customer, quantity, and date.","source":{"title":"Record special sales prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-record-sales-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-173","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant sets up a special sales price for an item that should only apply when a customer buys at least 100 units. Which field on the price line enforces this condition?","options":["Unit of Measure Code","Ending Date","Sales Type","Minimum Quantity"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Minimum Quantity field on a sales price line makes the special price valid only when the quantity ordered meets or exceeds the specified amount.","source":{"title":"Record special sales prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-record-sales-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-174","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A special sales price should apply to every customer that belongs to a particular customer price group rather than to a single customer. When creating the price, what should the consultant select as the applies-to (sales) type?","options":["Customer Price Group","All Customers","Campaign","Customer"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Choosing Customer Price Group as the sales type applies the special price to all customers assigned to that price group, avoiding per-customer maintenance.","source":{"title":"Record special sales prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-record-sales-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-175","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A vendor grants a lower purchase price on an item only between specific dates for a promotion. Which fields on the purchase price line should the consultant use to limit the price to that window?","options":["Minimum Quantity and Unit of Measure","Starting Date and Ending Date","Vendor No. and Currency Code","Line Discount % and Direct Unit Cost"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Starting Date and Ending Date fields restrict when a special purchase price is valid, so the promotional cost applies only within the defined period.","source":{"title":"Record special purchase prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchase-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-176","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Where does a purchase line discount that a vendor grants come from when a purchase order line is entered for an item?","options":["The item's inventory posting setup","The general ledger setup","A purchase line discount agreement defined for the vendor and item","The vendor's payment terms"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Purchase line discounts are recorded as agreements per vendor and item (with optional quantity/date conditions) and are applied automatically to matching purchase lines.","source":{"title":"Record special purchase prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchase-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-177","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants purchase invoice discounts, once calculated on purchase documents, to be posted to a separate general ledger account. Which action is required to enable invoice discounts to be calculated on purchases?","options":["Enable Calc. Inv. Discount in Purchases & Payables Setup","Assign a vendor price group to each vendor","Turn off the Adjust for Payment Discount option","Create a recurring purchase journal"],"correct":[0],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Calc. Inv. Discount setting (in Purchases & Payables Setup) automatically calculates the invoice discount when documents are updated, based on the vendor's invoice discount terms.","source":{"title":"Record special purchase prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchase-price-discount-payment-agreements"}},{"id":"gen-178","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In the new pricing experience, a consultant creates a single price list that contains both special unit prices and line discounts for a customer. Which price list setting controls whether the lines define prices, discounts, or both?","options":["The Status field","The Currency Code field","The Amount Type (Defines) field","The Assign-to Type field"],"correct":[2],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Amount Type field (what the list defines) can be set to Price, Discount, or Any, letting one price list hold price lines, discount lines, or both.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"gen-179","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A newly created price list is not yet affecting any documents. Which price list status must be set so that its prices and discounts become effective on sales and purchase lines?","options":["Draft","Active","Archived","Blocked"],"correct":[1],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A price list only influences documents once its Status is set to Active; Draft lists are still being edited and are not applied.","source":{"title":"Set up prices and discounts — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-prices-and-discounts"}},{"id":"gen-180","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to record that a customer always pays in a foreign currency and should see prices in that currency on documents. Which customer card field ensures new sales documents default to that currency?","options":["Location Code","Customer Posting Group","Language Code","Currency Code"],"correct":[3],"skill":3,"sub":"3.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Currency Code on the customer card sets the default currency for the customer's sales documents, so amounts and applicable prices are shown in that currency.","source":{"title":"Register new customers by creating a Customer Card — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-register-new-customers"}},{"id":"gen-181","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user wants to add a field that is normally hidden to their Customer Card and move it above the existing fields, but only for their own account. Which feature should they use?","options":["Designer, opened from the Settings (gear) menu","Personalize, opened from the Settings (gear) menu","Configuration Package import","Profile (Role) customization by an administrator"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Personalize (Settings gear > Personalize) changes the page only for the current user, letting them add hidden fields, move, or hide elements. Designer changes the page for everyone assigned to the profile.","source":{"title":"Personalize your workspace — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-personalization-user"}},{"id":"gen-182","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After personalizing several pages, a user finds the changes confusing and wants to revert one specific page back to how it appears for their role by default. What is the correct action?","options":["On the personalized page, choose Personalize, then Clear personalization","Sign out and sign back in to reset all pages","Ask an administrator to reassign the user's profile","Delete and recreate the user account"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"While in personalization mode on a page, choosing Clear personalization removes the user's customizations for that page and restores the profile default. It affects only the current page and user.","source":{"title":"Personalize your workspace — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-personalization-user"}},{"id":"gen-183","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user wants the first two columns of a wide list page to remain visible while scrolling horizontally through the other columns. Which personalization capability accomplishes this?","options":["Hide the extra columns","Add the columns to the FactBox pane","Set the freeze pane on a chosen column","Move the columns to a new FastTab"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Personalization lets a user set the freeze pane so that columns to the left of the chosen column stay in view while scrolling horizontally. It is set from the column's personalization menu.","source":{"title":"Personalize your workspace — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-personalization-user"}},{"id":"gen-184","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which statement correctly distinguishes Personalize from Designer in Business Central?","options":["Personalize changes pages for all users of a profile; Designer changes them for one user","Both features change pages only for the current user","Both features require a developer license to use","Personalize changes pages only for the current user; Designer changes them for everyone assigned to the profile"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Personalize affects only the signed-in user's experience, whereas Designer (profile customization) applies changes to all users assigned to that profile.","source":{"title":"Personalize your workspace — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-personalization-user"}},{"id":"gen-185","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to filter the Customer list to show only customers with a high outstanding balance. In the filter field, which operator returns records where Balance (LCY) is greater than 10000?","options":["=10000",">10000","|10000","@10000"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The greater-than operator (>) filters for values above the specified number. The @ operator makes a text filter case-insensitive, and | means OR.","source":{"title":"Sort, search, and filter data — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-enter-criteria-filters"}},{"id":"gen-186","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user needs to filter posted sales invoices to those posted between January 1 and March 31, 2026. Which filter expression entered in the Posting Date field is correct?","options":["01/01/2026|03/31/2026","01/01/2026&03/31/2026","01/01/2026*03/31/2026","01/01/2026..03/31/2026"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The range operator (..) filters for all values between and including the two endpoints, making it the standard way to filter a date interval.","source":{"title":"Sort, search, and filter data — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-enter-criteria-filters"}},{"id":"gen-187","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In a filter field, a user types the token %mytoday. What does this filter token represent?","options":["The last date the record was modified","The work date set in Business Central","The current calendar date (today)","The first day of the current accounting period"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Filter tokens such as %mytoday resolve to a dynamic value; %mytoday returns today's calendar date. Business Central also offers tokens like %me for the current user.","source":{"title":"Sort, search, and filter data — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-enter-criteria-filters"}},{"id":"gen-188","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user has applied several column filters plus a sort order to the Items list and wants to keep this configuration available to reuse later from the navigation pane. What should they do?","options":["Save the filtered result as a new view","Export the list to Excel and reopen it each time","Personalize the page to hide non-matching rows","Create a configuration package for the Item table"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"After applying filters and sorting, a user can save the configuration as a view, which then appears in the page's view list for quick reuse.","source":{"title":"Sort, search, and filter data — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-enter-criteria-filters"}},{"id":"gen-189","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"On a list, a user wants records where the Country/Region Code is either US or CA. Which single filter expression returns both?","options":["US..CA","US&CA","US|CA","US*CA"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The pipe (|) operator means OR, returning records matching either value. The ampersand (&) means AND, which for a single field would return no records.","source":{"title":"Sort, search, and filter data — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-enter-criteria-filters"}},{"id":"gen-190","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"What is the difference between the Search (magnifying glass) box on a list page and applying a filter?","options":["Search permanently changes the underlying table data; filtering does not","Search looks across visible columns for matching text without defining field criteria; a filter targets specific fields with defined criteria","Search can only be used by administrators; filtering is available to all users","Search and filter are identical and interchangeable terms"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Search box quickly narrows a list by matching typed text across the visible columns, while filtering lets you define precise criteria on specific fields.","source":{"title":"Sort, search, and filter data — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-enter-criteria-filters"}},{"id":"gen-191","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A controller wants to analyze the Item Ledger Entries list interactively, grouping by Location and pivoting quantities, without leaving Business Central or writing a report. Which feature should they turn on?","options":["Edit in Excel","Designer","The Job Queue","Data analysis mode (Analyze action)"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Data analysis mode, started with the Analyze action, lets users pivot, group, and summarize list data directly in the browser without running a report or exporting.","source":{"title":"Analyze data using data analysis mode — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/analysis-mode"}},{"id":"gen-192","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When working in data analysis mode on a list page, how are the changes a user makes (columns, pivots, filters) stored?","options":["They are saved as analysis tabs that are personal to the user and do not change the posted data","They overwrite the shared page layout for all users","They post directly to the general ledger","They are discarded and cannot be revisited"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Data analysis mode lets users create multiple analysis tabs that are personal to them; the underlying records are never modified by the analysis.","source":{"title":"Analyze data using data analysis mode — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/analysis-mode"}},{"id":"gen-193","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"In data analysis mode, a user drags a numeric field into the area that aggregates values (sum, average, count) across the row and column groupings. This area is best described as which of the following?","options":["The Filter columns area","The Row groups area","The Values (data) area of the pivot","The Search box"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"In pivot mode, numeric fields placed in the Values area are aggregated (for example summed) across the chosen row and column groupings.","source":{"title":"Analyze data using data analysis mode — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/analysis-mode"}},{"id":"gen-194","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user chooses Edit in Excel from the Customers list, changes several customers' credit limits in the workbook, and clicks Publish in the Excel add-in. What happens?","options":["A static snapshot is created and the changes stay only in Excel","Nothing until an administrator imports the file manually","The Excel file is emailed to the user for offline storage","The changed values are written back to Business Central through the add-in"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Edit in Excel uses the Business Central Excel add-in; when the user chooses Publish, the edited rows are written back to Business Central, subject to their permissions.","source":{"title":"Viewing and editing in Excel — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-work-with-excel"}},{"id":"gen-195","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Which statement correctly contrasts Open in Excel with Edit in Excel?","options":["Open in Excel exports a static copy you cannot publish back; Edit in Excel uses the add-in so changes can be published back to Business Central","Open in Excel writes changes back; Edit in Excel only exports a static copy","Both actions always write changes back to Business Central","Neither action requires an Excel license or the add-in"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Open in Excel produces a static export for viewing or offline use, while Edit in Excel opens the workbook with the add-in that lets you publish edits back to Business Central.","source":{"title":"Viewing and editing in Excel — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-work-with-excel"}},{"id":"gen-196","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user exports a filtered list using Edit in Excel. Which of the following is true about the filters and permissions in the resulting workbook?","options":["All filters are removed so the full table is exported regardless of the user's permissions","The current filters are respected, and publishing back is still governed by the user's Business Central permissions","The workbook grants the user full write access ignoring their permission sets","Only the columns the user hid on the page are exported"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Edit in Excel carries over the filters applied on the page, and any changes published back are still subject to the user's normal Business Central permissions.","source":{"title":"Viewing and editing in Excel — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/across-work-with-excel"}},{"id":"gen-197","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A user is reviewing a posted purchase invoice and wants to see all the G/L, VAT, and item ledger entries that resulted from posting that specific document. Which action should they use?","options":["Personalize","Edit in Excel","Analyze","Find Entries"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Find Entries (Navigate) lists all ledger and register entries created by posting a specific document, letting the user drill into the related G/L, VAT, and item entries.","source":{"title":"Finding Related Entries for Documents — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-find-entries"}},{"id":"gen-198","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The Find Entries feature locates related entries by matching which key piece of information from the posted document?","options":["The document number (and posting date) recorded on the entries","The color theme selected by the user","The user's personalization settings","The saved view applied to the list"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.1","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Find Entries retrieves related entries by matching the document number (together with posting information) that was stamped on the ledger entries when the document was posted.","source":{"title":"Finding Related Entries for Documents — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-find-entries"}},{"id":"gen-199","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A sales representative has entered a sales quote for a prospective customer who now wants to proceed with the purchase. The consultant wants the quote data carried into an editable order without re-keying the lines. Which action should the representative use on the sales quote?","options":["Post the quote directly to create a shipment","Choose Make Order to convert the quote into a sales order","Run Combine Shipments to group the quote lines","Use Copy Document into a posted sales invoice"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A sales quote is a non-posting document; choosing Make Order converts it into a sales order, deleting the quote and carrying its lines over so the order can be shipped and invoiced.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage sales — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-manage-sales"}},{"id":"gen-200","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When posting a sales order, the user is prompted to choose how to post the document. Which posting option records the goods leaving inventory and the customer invoice in a single step?","options":["Ship","Receive","Ship and Invoice","Invoice"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Posting a sales order with Ship and Invoice creates the posted sales shipment and the posted sales invoice at once, while Ship only records the delivery and Invoice only records the billing.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage sales — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-manage-sales"}},{"id":"gen-201","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer has committed to buying a large quantity of an item over the coming year, to be delivered in several partial shipments against agreed terms. Which document should the consultant recommend as the framework agreement from which individual sales orders are created?","options":["A sales blanket order","A recurring sales invoice","A sales return order","A standard sales quote"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A blanket sales order represents a long-term agreement for a total quantity; individual sales orders are generated from its lines for each partial delivery.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage sales — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-manage-sales"}},{"id":"gen-202","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Several sales orders have been shipped but not yet invoiced for the same customer during the month. The customer wants a single monthly invoice covering all the deliveries. Which function should be used?","options":["Get Shipment Lines on each order","Copy Document from each order into one order","Make Order on the sales quotes","Combine Shipments to create one invoice from multiple posted shipments"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Combine Shipments batch job gathers posted, uninvoiced sales shipment lines for a customer into one sales invoice, reducing the number of invoices sent.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage sales — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-manage-sales"}},{"id":"gen-203","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A purchasing agent receives goods physically before the vendor's invoice arrives. Using a purchase order, how should the agent record only the physical receipt of the items at this point?","options":["Post the order with the Invoice option","Post the order with the Receive option","Create a purchase credit memo","Post the order with Receive and Invoice"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Posting a purchase order with Receive records the items into inventory and creates a posted purchase receipt; the vendor invoice can be posted later when it arrives.","source":{"title":"Record purchases with purchase invoices — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchases"}},{"id":"gen-204","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A warehouse worker occasionally receives slightly more than the ordered quantity from a trusted vendor and the company wants to allow this within tolerance without blocking the receipt. Which configuration enables posting a receipt for more than the ordered quantity?","options":["An over-receipt code with an allowed over-receipt tolerance","A blanket purchase order","A purchase return order","A prepayment percentage on the vendor"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Over-receipt codes define an allowed percentage by which the received quantity may exceed the ordered quantity, letting warehouse staff post the larger receipt within tolerance.","source":{"title":"Record purchases with purchase invoices — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchases"}},{"id":"gen-205","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"The difference between a purchase invoice and a purchase order in Business Central most directly concerns which capability?","options":["Only purchase invoices can reference a vendor","A purchase invoice cannot post to the general ledger","A purchase order cannot include item charges","A purchase order supports partial receipts and invoicing over time, whereas a purchase invoice records receipt and invoicing together"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Purchase orders are used when receipts and invoices happen at different times or in parts; a purchase invoice records the receipt and the invoice in one posting, so it suits simpler purchases.","source":{"title":"Record purchases with purchase invoices — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchases"}},{"id":"gen-206","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A vendor sends multiple deliveries against one purchase order, and the accounts payable clerk later wants to invoice several posted receipts on a single purchase invoice. Which action supports this?","options":["Combine Return Receipts","Get Receipt Lines to pull posted receipt lines into a purchase invoice","Make Order on the purchase quote","Post the receipts with the Invoice option only"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"On a purchase invoice, the Get Receipt Lines function inserts lines from one or more posted purchase receipts so multiple deliveries can be invoiced together.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage purchasing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-manage-purchasing"}},{"id":"gen-207","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant must configure a sales order so the customer is billed 25% of the order value before any goods are shipped. Where is the 25% most efficiently defined so it defaults onto the order lines?","options":["In the General Ledger Setup","In the number series for sales orders","On the item's costing method","As a Prepayment % on the customer card or a prepayment sales price setup"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A default Prepayment % can be set on the customer card (or via prepayment price setup), so it flows to the sales order lines and drives how much is invoiced in advance.","source":{"title":"Invoice prepayments — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-invoice-prepayments"}},{"id":"gen-208","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When a prepayment invoice is posted for a sales order, to which account is the prepayment amount posted until the final invoice is issued?","options":["Directly to the sales revenue account","To the inventory account","To a prepayment (unrealized/liability) account defined in the posting setup","To the customer's fixed asset account"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Prepayment invoices post to a dedicated prepayment account specified in the General Posting Setup, holding the amount as a liability until the final invoice recognizes the revenue.","source":{"title":"Invoice prepayments — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-invoice-prepayments"}},{"id":"gen-209","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After a prepayment invoice was posted on a sales order, the customer renegotiates and the prepaid amount must be reduced. The order has not yet been fully invoiced. What is the correct way to reverse the excess prepayment?","options":["Delete the sales order and start over","Post a prepayment credit memo for the order to correct the prepaid amount","Manually edit the posted prepayment invoice","Post the final invoice and ignore the difference"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Business Central lets you post a prepayment credit memo from the order to reverse or correct a previously invoiced prepayment; posted invoices cannot be edited directly.","source":{"title":"Invoice prepayments — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-invoice-prepayments"}},{"id":"gen-210","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A customer wants to return goods from a completed sale, and the company needs to manage the physical return receipt into inventory as well as the credit. Which document is most appropriate?","options":["A sales quote","A blanket sales order","A purchase credit memo","A sales return order"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A sales return order supports receiving returned items into inventory and creating the related sales credit memo, making it the right tool when goods physically come back.","source":{"title":"Process sales returns or cancellations — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-process-sales-returns-cancellations"}},{"id":"gen-211","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A posted sales invoice was created in error and no payment has been applied. The consultant wants Business Central to automatically create and post a corrective credit memo that reverses the entries. Which function should be used from the posted sales invoice?","options":["Copy Document","Cancel (or Correct)","Combine Shipments","Make Order"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Cancel and Correct functions on a posted sales invoice automatically generate and post a corrective sales credit memo that reverses the invoice, provided it can still be corrected.","source":{"title":"Process sales returns or cancellations — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-process-sales-returns-cancellations"}},{"id":"gen-212","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company processes many customer returns and wants to consolidate several posted return receipts onto a single sales credit memo. Which function accomplishes this?","options":["Combine Return Receipts","Get Shipment Lines","Suggest Vendor Payments","Make Order"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Combine Return Receipts batch job groups posted return receipt lines for a customer onto one sales credit memo, mirroring how Combine Shipments works for outbound sales.","source":{"title":"Process sales returns or cancellations — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/sales-how-process-sales-returns-cancellations"}},{"id":"gen-213","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A purchasing manager needs to return defective items to a vendor and receive a credit, including tracking the physical shipment of goods back to the vendor. Which document should be used?","options":["A purchase quote","A sales return order","A purchase return order","A general journal line"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A purchase return order manages shipping items back to the vendor and generating the purchase credit memo, making it the correct choice for vendor returns involving physical goods.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage purchasing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-manage-purchasing"}},{"id":"gen-214","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant wants to speed up entry of a new purchase order that is nearly identical to one posted last month. Which function copies the lines and header details from the existing document into the new one?","options":["Copy Document","Combine Receipts","Get Receipt Lines","Cancel"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Copy Document function lets you reuse header and line information from an existing or posted purchase document to quickly create a new one.","source":{"title":"Overview of tasks to manage purchasing — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-manage-purchasing"}},{"id":"gen-215","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Before any prepayment invoice can be posted, Business Central requires that a prepayment account is available for the item's posting configuration. Where must this prepayment account be specified for sales and purchases?","options":["In the customer or vendor bank account card","In the number series lines","In the depreciation book","In the General Posting Setup for the relevant business/product posting group combination"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Prepayment accounts (Sales Prepayments Account and Purch. Prepayments Account) are defined in the General Posting Setup per business and product posting group combination, and posting fails if they are missing.","source":{"title":"Invoice prepayments — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/finance-invoice-prepayments"}},{"id":"gen-216","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A small supplier bills and delivers at the same time, so the accountant does not need to track a separate order and receipt. Which document lets them record the purchase, receive the goods, and post the vendor invoice in one step?","options":["A blanket purchase order","A purchase quote","A purchase invoice","A purchase return order"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.2","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A purchase invoice records the vendor's charge and the receipt of items together in a single posting, which suits straightforward purchases with no need for partial receipts.","source":{"title":"Record purchases with purchase invoices — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/purchasing-how-record-purchases"}},{"id":"gen-217","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is registering a newly purchased machine as a fixed asset in Business Central and wants to record its acquisition cost. Before the acquisition can be posted, which requirement must be satisfied for the asset?","options":["The asset must first be fully depreciated in a prior book","The asset must already have a posted disposal entry","A physical inventory journal must be posted for the asset","At least one depreciation book must be assigned to the fixed asset"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"You cannot post any FA transaction, including acquisition, until the fixed asset has a depreciation book assigned to it, because the depreciation book defines how amounts are posted for that asset.","source":{"title":"Acquire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-acquire"}},{"id":"gen-218","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An accountant wants to post the acquisition cost of several fixed assets quickly without creating purchase invoices. Which tool in Business Central lets them post acquisition costs directly to the assets?","options":["The Fixed Asset G/L Journal","The Sales Order page","The Payment Reconciliation Journal","The Physical Inventory Journal"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Acquisition costs can be posted through the Fixed Asset G/L Journal (or via the Acquisition assisted setup), which posts to both the FA ledger and the general ledger.","source":{"title":"Acquire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-acquire"}},{"id":"gen-219","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"When posting the acquisition of a fixed asset, a consultant wants the amount to be treated as the initial cost basis for depreciation. Which FA Posting Type should the journal line use?","options":["Depreciation","Write-Down","Acquisition Cost","Salvage Value"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Acquisition Cost FA Posting Type records the asset's cost basis, which is the amount depreciation is subsequently calculated against.","source":{"title":"Acquire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-acquire"}},{"id":"gen-220","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company wants a portion of an asset's cost to be excluded from depreciation because it represents the estimated residual value at the end of the asset's life. Which field on the FA acquisition should be used?","options":["Write-Down Amount","Custom 1 Amount","Maintenance Amount","Salvage Value"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Salvage value represents the residual value at the end of an asset's useful life and is deducted so that depreciation is calculated only on the depreciable base.","source":{"title":"Acquire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-acquire"}},{"id":"gen-221","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"At month-end, an accountant needs to calculate and post depreciation for many fixed assets at once. Which feature should they use?","options":["The Adjust Cost - Item Entries batch job","The Suggest Vendor Payments batch job","The Calculate Depreciation batch job","The Close Income Statement batch job"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Calculate Depreciation batch job computes depreciation for the selected assets and fills FA journal (or FA G/L journal) lines that you then post.","source":{"title":"Depreciate or amortize fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-depreciate-amortize"}},{"id":"gen-222","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"After running the Calculate Depreciation batch job, an accountant reviews the created journal lines but the depreciation has not yet affected the ledgers. What must they do to complete the process?","options":["Run the batch job a second time","Assign a new depreciation book to each asset","Reverse the acquisition entries first","Post the resulting FA journal (or FA G/L journal) lines"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Calculate Depreciation only fills the journal lines; you must post those lines for the depreciation to update the FA ledger and general ledger.","source":{"title":"Depreciate or amortize fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-depreciate-amortize"}},{"id":"gen-223","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant sets up a depreciation book so that each depreciation posting also generates a corresponding entry in the general ledger. Which depreciation book setting controls this behavior?","options":["The G/L Integration - Depreciation option must be enabled","The Allow Correction of Disposal option must be enabled","The Use FA Ledger Check option must be disabled","The Allow Depreciation Below Zero option must be enabled"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"G/L integration settings on the depreciation book determine which FA posting types (such as depreciation) also post to the general ledger; without integration, entries stay only in the FA ledger.","source":{"title":"Depreciate or amortize fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-depreciate-amortize"}},{"id":"gen-224","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A fixed asset's depreciation must be split so that different departments each carry part of the expense. Which FA depreciation book feature supports posting depreciation to multiple accounts or dimensions?","options":["FA reclassification journal","The Salvage Value field","FA allocation keys (allocation percentages)","Item charge assignment"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"FA allocation keys let depreciation (and other FA amounts) be distributed by percentage across accounts or dimensions such as departments.","source":{"title":"Depreciate or amortize fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-depreciate-amortize"}},{"id":"gen-225","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company sells a fixed asset and needs Business Central to automatically calculate the gain or loss on the sale. What determines the gain or loss amount when the disposal is posted?","options":["The difference between the sales proceeds and the asset's net book value","The total acquisition cost only, regardless of depreciation","The salvage value entered at acquisition","The vendor's original invoice amount"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"On disposal, Business Central compares the sales proceeds to the asset's net book value (acquisition cost less accumulated depreciation) to compute the gain or loss.","source":{"title":"Dispose of or retire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-dispose-retire"}},{"id":"gen-226","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An accountant needs to record that a fixed asset was scrapped with no sales value. Which FA Posting Type is used to record the disposal transaction?","options":["Acquisition Cost","Maintenance","Disposal","Write-Down"],"correct":[2],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Disposal FA Posting Type records the retirement or sale of an asset; entering proceeds of zero records a scrapped asset and posts the resulting loss.","source":{"title":"Dispose of or retire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-dispose-retire"}},{"id":"gen-227","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is told that Business Central rejects a disposal posting because the asset has not been fully acquired in the depreciation book being used. What is the general rule for disposing of a fixed asset?","options":["The asset must be disposed of in a separate company","Depreciation must be turned off for the book first","The asset must be transferred to a new FA class before disposal","The acquisition cost must be posted before a disposal can be recorded"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"An asset must first have its acquisition cost posted (and normally be depreciated up to date) before a disposal entry can be posted in that depreciation book.","source":{"title":"Dispose of or retire fixed assets — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/fa-how-dispose-retire"}},{"id":"gen-228","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A warehouse manager counts physical stock and finds discrepancies against the quantities recorded in Business Central. Which journal is designed to record the counted quantities and post the resulting adjustments?","options":["The Physical Inventory Journal","The Recurring General Journal","The Cash Receipt Journal","The FA G/L Journal"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Physical Inventory Journal captures counted quantities against calculated on-hand and posts positive or negative adjustments to reconcile inventory.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"gen-229","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"Before entering counted quantities in the Physical Inventory Journal, an accountant wants the system to populate each line with the quantity currently recorded on hand. Which action should they run?","options":["Adjust Cost - Item Entries","Calculate Inventory","Suggest Item Journal Lines","Post Inventory Cost to G/L"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Calculate Inventory action fills the physical inventory journal with items and their recorded quantities so the counter can enter the actual counted amounts alongside them.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"gen-230","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant needs to change the bin and location recorded for some items without altering the total quantity on hand or posting a value adjustment. Which journal should they use?","options":["The Item Reclassification Journal","The Physical Inventory Journal","The Revaluation Journal","The Item Journal with a positive adjustment"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Item Reclassification Journal moves items between dimensions such as location, bin, or variant without changing overall quantity or cost.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"gen-231","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"An accountant notices that inventory value in the general ledger does not reflect recent purchase and sales transactions because actual costs were only known later. Which process recalculates and forwards actual costs to inventory value?","options":["The Calculate Depreciation batch job","The Adjust Cost - Item Entries batch job","The Delete Invoiced Sales Orders batch job","The Calculate Inventory batch job"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"The Adjust Cost - Item Entries batch job recalculates actual costs of inventory and forwards cost changes to related entries so that inventory value is correct.","source":{"title":"Count, adjust, and reclassify inventory — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-count-adjust-reclassify"}},{"id":"gen-232","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A company moves goods between two warehouse locations and wants the goods tracked as in-transit while they are being moved. Which document should the consultant recommend?","options":["A sales order","A transfer order","An item journal positive adjustment","A purchase return order"],"correct":[1],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A transfer order moves items from one location to another and uses an in-transit location so the goods are tracked while being shipped and before being received.","source":{"title":"Transfer inventory between locations — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-transfer-between-locations"}},{"id":"gen-233","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A consultant is configuring a transfer order between two locations. Which setup element is required so that goods can be recorded as shipped from one location before they arrive at the other?","options":["A blocked item variant","A fixed asset posting group","A payment method code","An in-transit location code"],"correct":[3],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"Transfer orders require an in-transit location, which holds the goods between shipment from the source location and receipt at the destination location.","source":{"title":"Transfer inventory between locations — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-transfer-between-locations"}},{"id":"gen-234","sourceBank":"microsoft-learn","type":"single","generated":true,"question":"A small company moves goods between two nearby locations and does not want to track goods in transit, preferring the transfer to ship and receive in a single step. Which approach supports this?","options":["Use a direct transfer instead of a standard transfer order","Post a sales invoice between the two locations","Use the Physical Inventory Journal at both locations","Assign a new depreciation book to the items"],"correct":[0],"skill":4,"sub":"4.3","confidence":"high","set":null,"section":null,"topic":null,"explanation":"A direct transfer moves items directly from one location to another in a single posting without using an in-transit location, suitable when goods do not need to be tracked while moving.","source":{"title":"Transfer inventory between locations — Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/inventory-how-transfer-between-locations"}}];
